\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Global  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Falls sharply against the Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 440 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollar retreated against global peers on Wednesday after the August producer price index (PPI) moderated concerns about inflation in the U.S., a day after a surprisingly high consumer inflation reading in the country. Overall, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's retreat was modest except when compared with the yen, which strengthened amid speculation about \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BoJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation.\par \par \uc2 The DXY index, which compares the dollar against a basket of six strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was down 0.14% at 109.658 points. By late afternoon in New York, the dollar was down at 143.17 yen, the euro appreciated to $0.9975 and the pound rose to $1.1537.\par \par \uc2 Hurt by the interest rate differential between Japan and other developed economies such as the U.S., the euro zone and the U.K., the yen recently hit its lowest level against the dollar in 24 years and has already accumulated a drop of more than 20% in 2022. Worried about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movement, the BoJ and the Japanese government are considering the option to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange rate, as said the Japanese Finance Minister, \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2 . He further stated that any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be done in an agile manner.\par \par \uc2 Even though the yen has strengthened in the face of the news, it is "questionable at best how effective the plans will be in the face of a widening interest rate differential," Capital Economics weighs in. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have an uneven track record and were not very effective the last time they were attempted during the Asian financial crisis (in 1997). Yen turnover in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has tripled since then. Academic evidence suggests less success if \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  go against the market trend, which would be the case here," summarizes the consulting firm.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, the dollar rally after the reading of the August CPI lost steam today, says analyst Joe Manimbo, from Convera. The American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deepened its fall earlier, after the U.S. PPI for this month showed an expected slight deflation compared to July.\par \par \uc2 Also out came UK consumer inflation data, which slowed to 9.9% year-on-year in August.\par \par \uc2 ING expects the British CPI to accelerate in the coming months to a peak of 11%. Next week is the next meeting of the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  (\uc2 BoE\uc2 ), which should mark another interest rate hike in the UK. ING projects another hike of 50 basis points, but warns that an adjustment of 75 basis points, as the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 ECB\uc2 ) did, cannot be ruled out.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220915ei9e000nw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
