\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen rallies vs dollar after \uc2 BOJ\uc2  rate check, hints on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , U.S. PPI data\b0\par\par\uc2 845 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par 22:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Updates to late New York afternoon)\par     By Caroline Valetkevitch\par     NEW YORK, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The yen rose 1% against the dollar on Wednesday after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par conducted a rate check in possible preparation for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while investors digested U.S.\par producer prices data.\par     In a rate check, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials call up dealers and ask for the price of buying or selling yen.\par However, actually \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be a larger step.\par     Japanese Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shunichi Suzuki\f28 \uc2 \f2  told reporters on Wednesday that recent yen moves have been\par "rapid and one-sided", adding that yen-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was among the government's options\par should such moves continue.\par     "Most market participants are on pins and needles awaiting whether or not we're going to get any sort of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 ministry of finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Bipan Rai, North American head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at\par CIBC Capital Markets in Toronto.\par     "It's one of those things where we've seen comments so many times about the fact that they're watching\par and monitoring the yen. The fact that they did a rate check overnight kind of indicates we're in greater\par proximity toward \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But just \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by itself we don't think is going to be all that\par successful outside of an immediate knee-jerk reaction."\par     The recent sharp gains in the dollar versus the yen have been tied to the hawkish stance from the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  in raising interest rates to control inflation. The dollar hit a 24-year peak against the\par yen last week.\par     The dollar dropped against the yen right after news of the rate check. Nikkei website reported the rate\par check, citing unidentified sources, and Reuters later confirmed it with a market source. It was last down 1%\par  at 143.19 yen, hitting a session low of 142.6 in the wake of the PPI data. \par     The dollar index, which tracks the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against six main peers, was down 0.1% on Wednesday at\par 109.71, a day after registering its largest daily percentage gain since March 2020 on an unexpected rise in\par the U.S. consumer price index (CPI). \par     On Wednesday, investors weighed data showing U.S. producer prices fell for second straight month in\par August. It also showed underlying producer inflation rising moderately last month.\par     Financial markets now have fully priced in an interest rate hike of at least 75 basis points at the\par conclusion of the Fed's policy meeting next week, according to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 CME\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Fedwatch tool. \par     As inflation is a small concern in Japan, authorities are keeping yields on Japanese government bonds\par pinned down to help with the economic recovery.\par     The two-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yield, a bellwether for interest rate expectations, rose another\par 2.2 basis points (bps) to 3.778% Wednesday after jumping 18.5 bps on Tuesday following the consumer price\par data.\par     The euro was nearly flat against the dollar at $0.9972, while sterling was up 0.4%\par against the dollar at $1.1534.\par     The U.S. dollar was up 0.1% against the Swiss franc. \par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 3:42PM (1942 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct       High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                   \par                                               Session                                             \par  Dollar index                 109.7100       109.8300    -0.09%         14.684%       +109.9300   +109.2700\par  Euro/Dollar                  $0.9972        $0.9968     +0.04%         -12.28%       +$1.0024    +$0.9956\par  Dollar/Yen                   143.1850       144.6200    -0.99%         +24.39%       +144.9550   +142.5550\par  Euro/Yen                     142.77         144.08      -0.91%         +9.55%        +144.4700   +142.3000\par  Dollar/Swiss                 0.9634         0.9619      +0.12%         +5.57%        +0.9636     +0.9591\par  Sterling/Dollar              $1.1534        $1.1494     +0.35%         -14.71%       +$1.1589    +$1.1480\par  Dollar/Canadian              1.3182         1.3175      +0.06%         +4.26%        +1.3206     +1.3139\par  Aussie/Dollar                $0.6737        $0.6733     +0.06%         -7.32%        +$0.6760    +$0.6705\par  Euro/Swiss                   0.9605         0.9583      +0.23%         -7.37%        +0.9628     +0.9582\par  Euro/Sterling                0.8643         0.8674      -0.36%         +2.