\par\par \b \uc2 Yen rallies vs dollar after \uc2 BOJ\uc2  rate check, hints on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , U.S. PPI data\b0\par\par\uc2 835 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par 22:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Reuters) - The yen rose 1% against the dollar on Wednesday after the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted a rate check in possible preparation for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while investors digested U.S. producer prices data.\par \par \uc2 In a rate check, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials call up dealers and ask for the price of buying or selling yen. However, actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be a larger step.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  told reporters on Wednesday that recent yen moves have been "rapid and one-sided", adding that yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was among the government's options should such moves continue.\par \par \uc2 "Most market participants are on pins and needles awaiting whether or not we're going to get any sort of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Bipan Rai, North American head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at CIBC Capital Markets in Toronto.\par \par \uc2 "It's one of those things where we've seen comments so many times about the fact that they're watching and monitoring the yen. The fact that they did a rate check overnight kind of indicates we're in greater proximity toward \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But just \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by itself we don't think is going to be all that successful outside of an immediate knee-jerk reaction."\par \par \uc2 The recent sharp gains in the dollar versus the yen have been tied to the hawkish stance from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  in raising interest rates to control inflation. The dollar hit a 24-year peak against the yen last week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar dropped against the yen right after news of the rate check. Nikkei website reported the rate check, citing unidentified sources, and Reuters later confirmed it with a market source. It was last down 1% at 143.19 yen, hitting a session low of 142.6 in the wake of the PPI data.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which tracks the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against six main peers, was down 0.1% on Wednesday at 109.71, a day after registering its largest daily percentage gain since March 2020 on an unexpected rise in the U.S. consumer price index (CPI).\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, investors weighed data showing U.S. producer prices fell for second straight month in August. It also showed underlying producer inflation rising moderately last month.\par \par \uc2 Financial markets now have fully priced in an interest rate hike of at least 75 basis points at the conclusion of the Fed's policy meeting next week, according to the \uc2 CME\uc2 's Fedwatch tool.\par \par \uc2 As inflation is a small concern in Japan, authorities are keeping yields on Japanese government bonds pinned down to help with the economic recovery. [JP/T]\par \par \uc2 The two-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yield, a bellwether for interest rate expectations, rose another 2.2 basis points (bps) to 3.778% Wednesday after jumping 18.5 bps on Tuesday following the consumer price data.\par \par \uc2 The euro was nearly flat against the dollar at $0.9972, while sterling was up 0.4% against the dollar at $1.1534.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar was up 0.1% against the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 ======