\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen recovers lost ground on \uc2 Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  reports, hints at  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Kevin Buckland and Alun John\par \par \uc2 TOKYO/LONDON, Sep 14 (Reuters) - The yen climbed more than 1 percent on Wednesday after media reports that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  conducted a rate check in apparent preparation for an exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  tried to regain ground lost a day earlier against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The dollar lost more than 1% to 142.9 yen after the Nikkei website reported the rate check, citing unidentified sources. In a rate check, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials call traders and ask them the price to buy or sell yen.\par \par \uc2 * Reuters later confirmed the rate check with a market source.\par \par \uc2 * Earlier, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had weakened to a low of 144.97 yen per dollar, extending its sharp decline from the previous day when an unexpected rise in the U.S. consumer price index (CPI), which is likely to lead the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to an aggressive rate hike, sent the dollar soaring.\par \par \uc2 * The dollar index, which tracks the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against six major competitors, jumped 1.5% on Tuesday, its biggest daily percentage increase since March 2020.\par \par \uc2 * Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  told reporters Wednesday that the yen's recent moves have been "rapid and unilateral," adding that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy yen was among the government's options if such moves continued.\par \par \uc2 "If the market continues to sell yen, there is more pressure for the (Finance Ministry) and \uc2 BOJ\uc2  to communicate to the market that the recent move has been too quick," said Masayuki Kichikawa, chief macro strategist at Sumitomo Mitsui DS Asset Management.\par \par \uc2 * The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 24-year low of 144.99 units per dollar last week.\par \par \uc2 * Other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were still hunkered down after Tuesday's thrashing.\par \par \uc2 * The euro managed to climb back above parity to $1.0014, up 0.47%, but was still reeling from Tuesday's 1.5% drop, and was not far from last week's 20-year low of $0.9864.\par \par \uc2 * Sterling, which lost 1.6% on Tuesday, was up 0.43% at $1.1543 after lower fuel prices led to an unexpected drop in British inflation in August, according to figures released Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Buckland, Rae Wee and Alun John, Edited in Spanish by Manuel Far\u237\'00\'EDas)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220914ei9e006wc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
