\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen stems losses after report of \uc2 BOJ\uc2  rate check, hints on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 573 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par 10:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO/LONDON, Sept 14 (Reuters) - The yen rose on Wednesday, moving off a 24-year trough, after media reports that the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted a rate check, an apparent preparation for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while policymakers stepped up warnings about the yen's sharp fall.\par \par \uc2 The dollar slid 1% to 143 yen, after the Nikkei website cited unidentified sources for its report on the rate check, in which \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials call up dealers and ask for the price of buying or selling yen.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had softened near to 144.97 per dollar early in the day, having tumbled the day before along with other majors as an unexpected rise in the U.S. consumer price index (CPI) sent the greenback soaring.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index jumped 1.5% on Tuesday, its largest percentage gain since March 2020.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  also said on Wednesday that the government was considering stepping in to combat sharp falls in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been battered by a surging greenback.\par \par \uc2 Suzuki told reporters that recent moves in the yen have been "rapid and one-sided", adding that yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was among the government's options should such moves continue.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably considers recent moves in the yen rate as too sudden and too large," said Masayuki Kichikawa, chief macro strategist, Sumitomo Mitsui DS Asset Management.\par \par \uc2 "If the market continues to sell the yen, there is more pressure for the MOF and \uc2 BOJ\uc2  to communicate to the market that the recent move has been too fast."\par \par \uc2 However, actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  the support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would be a larger step.\par \par \uc2 "Currently, the dollar is becoming stronger and the yen weakening due to the big interest rate differentials between the United States and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so it's hard (for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to be effective. That's why I think it's better to wait," said Masafumi Yamamoto, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist, \uc2 Mizuho Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "If the dollar rises above 145 yen, the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will rise to about 60% from 10% to 20% before, rather than becoming 100%."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 24-year low of 144.99 last week.\par \par \uc2 The yield on two-year Treasury notes, which typically reflects interest rate expectations, peaked at 3.804% on Wednesday, the highest since 2007. The 10-year yield last stood at 3.4313%.\par \par \uc2 Financial markets now have fully priced in an interest rate hike of at least 75 bps at the conclusion of the FOMC's policy meeting next week, with a 38% probability of a super-sized, full percentage-point increase.\par \par \uc2 A day earlier, the probability of a 100 bps hike was zero.\par \par \uc2 Other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were still hunkered down after yesterday's battering, as a more aggressive pace of rate hikes in the U.S. and higher yields would likely support the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The euro was at $0.99935 up 0.25% but still reeling from Tuesdays 1.5% fall.\par \par \uc2 Sterling which lost 1.6% on Tuesday, was up 0.44% at $1.1545, after lower fuel prices caused an unexpected fall in British inflation in August, official figures showed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The risk-sensitive Aussie was flat at $0.67375, after a precipitous 2.26% slide overnight.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Buckland, Rae Wee and Alun John; Editing by Kim Coghill, Edmund Klamann and Toby Chopra) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-14T09:36:54.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220914ei9e01dox\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
