\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  revises exchange rates in apparent preparation for  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 757 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Kantaro Komiya and Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sep 14 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  has conducted a check on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in apparent preparation for a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Nikkei daily reported on Wednesday, as economic leaders stepped up warnings about sharp falls in the yen.\par \par \uc2 The yen was up slightly from a near 24-year low against the dollar after the report, which cited unidentified sources, and was trading around 143.89 at 0520 GMT.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has depreciated about 20% so far this year as the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (BoJ) has maintained a super-loose monetary policy at a time when many of its global counterparts, such as the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 , have aggressively raised interest rates to combat rising inflation, making Japanese assets less attractive to investors.\par \par \uc2 Aside from verbal warnings, Japanese authorities have several options to stem the yen's excessive slide. Among them is a rare direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling dollars and buying large amounts of yen.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BoJ\uc2 's exchange rate check, a practice in which \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  representatives call traders and ask the price at which to buy or sell the yen, is seen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as a possible precursor to \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 When the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  made its check, the exchange rate stood at around 144.9 per dollar, said the Jiji news agency, which based its information on a market source. The 145 mark is considered a key level for market watchers.\par \par \uc2 Many traders remained doubtful that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was imminent, but the jump in the yen pointed to increased jitters. The timing of the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's action also suggests that 145 per dollar will be an important level for markets and policymakers.\par \par \uc2 "My sense is that the Finance Ministry will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this point and leave it at verbal warnings," said \uc2 Takeshi Minami\uc2 , chief economist at the Norinchukin Institute for Analysis in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "There is still a week to go before the Fed's rate-setting meeting. I don't think markets believe the ministry will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current dollar/yen levels."\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  said earlier on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was among the options the government would consider.\par \par \uc2 Data released Tuesday showing unexpectedly strong U.S. inflation for the month of August prompted bets that the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  would raise interest rates and for longer, adding to downward pressure on the yen.\par \par \uc2 "The recent moves are rapid and one-sided, and we are very concerned. If these moves continue, we must respond without ruling out any options," Suzuki told reporters Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "We are talking about taking all available options, so it is correct to think like that," Suzuki said when asked if yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was among the government's options.\par \par \uc2 The comment was the strongest to date from government officials in signaling the possibility of monetary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which markets have nevertheless deemed highly unlikely due to the difficulty Tokyo would have in getting the go-ahead from its G7 partners.\par \par \uc2 Chief Cabinet Secretary \uc2 Hirokazu Matsuno\uc2  also said at a press conference on Wednesday that the government would take the necessary measures should excessive yen movements continue.\par \par \uc2 "We are very concerned about excessive volatility," Matsuno said.\par \par \uc2 Rob Carnell\uc2 , head of Asia-Pacific research at ING in Singapore, pointed to obstacles to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.\par \par \uc2 "Never say never. They've stepped up the rhetoric lately," he said. "But I would be cautious about the inevitability of their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a signatory to the G20 and has non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies."\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no intention of raising interest rates or changing its loose monetary policy in order to prop up the yen, three sources familiar with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's processes told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 The yen's weakness, once welcomed for giving a boost to exports, is becoming a headache for Japanese economic leaders as it hurts households and retailers by inflating already rising prices for fuel and imported food.\par \par \uc2 Yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been rare. The last time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in 1998, when the Asian financial crisis triggered a yen sell-off and a rapid capital outflow from the region. Before that, Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter the 1991-1992 yen plunge.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto and Leika Kihara; additional reporting by Kantaro Komiya, Daniel Leussink and Tom Westbrook; writing by Kim Coghill; editing by Neil Fullick and Bradley Perrett; translated by Tom\u225\'00\'E1s Cobos)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220914ei9e004l3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
