\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  does not rule out  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  to curb rapid yen devaluation\b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Suzuki has been "very concerned" about the "sudden" changes that the yen is experiencing, an "undesirable" trend that he believes is due to a "speculative movement" that worries the Executive, he told the media on public broadcaster NHK.\par \par \uc2 "If these movements continue, I think we have to respond to them without ruling out any options," said the minister, who, when asked specifically if they are thinking about market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the rapid devaluation of the yen, replied, "It is correct to think that is the case."\par \par \uc2 Suzuki's remarks are the latest in a series of comments from Japanese authorities over the yen's recent volatility and the rapid fall the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is experiencing this week amid fears of a tightening of the US \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy due to inflation, reports Efe.\par \par \uc2 The yen experienced high volatility today, from the mid-range of 143 units to the dollar to touch 144.96, touching the 145-unit barrier, a renewed 24-year low, before moderating its fall following statements from several high-profile officials, including government spokesman \uc2 Hirokazu Matsuno\uc2 . "It is important that exchange rates remain stable," Matsuno said, noting that they are keeping a close eye on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  developments.\par \par \uc2 The yen is under pressure from the prospect of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightening its monetary policy over inflation and distancing itself from the stance of its Japanese counterpart, which chooses to maintain its ultra-low interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The release of the latest U.S. price data, which showed a larger-than-expected rise, has only fueled this concern ahead of next week's \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  (Fed) and \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (BoJ) monetary policy meetings. This fear weighed on investors on the \uc2 Tokyo Stock Exchange\uc2  today, where in the absence of trading its main index, the Nikkei, was down 2.7%.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220914ei9e003ux\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
