8226\'20\'22 14:15 \uc2 ECB\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Lagarde presents the latest monetary policy decisions in Frankfurt \u8226\'20\'22 16:00 \uc2 Chicago Fed\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s Evans participates in discussion on current economic conditions or monetary policy in Glen Ellyn, Ill. Commentary and Analysis EUR/USD traders will very likely sell whatever \uc2 ECB\uc2  does \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD is entrenched in steep and growing decline \u8226\'20\'22 Pair began to fall moment taper talk emerged last year \u8226\'20\'22 Since May 2021 EUR/USD has dropped 1.2266-0.9864 \u8226\'20\'22 In recent months drop has sometimes become stretched (technically oversold) \u8226\'20\'22 Modest bounces (often close \uc2 ECB\uc2  meets) have been followed by deeper declines \u8226\'20\'22 The modest number current shorts represents little barrier to a bigger drop \u8226\'20\'22 Net short position is just $6 bln, circa 1/5 of the record short position \u8226\'20\'22 A bet in excess of $25 billion is probably needed to materially impact trend USD/JPY setback likely to be limited despite Japan's "warning" \u8226\'20\'22 Japan warns of action to stem 'speculative' yen moves \u8226\'20\'22 Spot's march higher stopped one pip ahead of 145.00 on Wednesday \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY has seen a wide 143.43-144.55 on Thursday, according to the EBS data \u8226\'20\'22 Daily points to bigger gains towards 1998 147.64 peak \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY rise to 150 might tip \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  scales \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/JPY usually makes gains in September \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/JPY's correlation with USD/JPY high, 30/60-day logs are above +0.50 GBP/USD by 1.15 pre-Truss plan after lift from 37-year low \u8226\'20\'22 Cable pivots 1.1500 after rallying off Wednesday's 37-year low of 1.1407 \u8226\'20\'22 Rally aided by lightening of USD long positions (1.1413 was March 2020 low) \u8226\'20\'22 1.1607 was Tuesday's high, before Truss succeeded Johnson as Britain's PM \u8226\'20\'22 Truss to set out 'bold' plan to tackle UK energy crisis \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 BoE\uc2  chief economist Pill said plan could slow UK inflation \u8226\'20\'22 Markets currently see 47% chance of 75 bps BoE hike Sept 15 vs 67% pre-Pill AUD/USD weighed down by dovish steer from \uc2 RBA\uc2  chief Lowe \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD fell to 0.6713 in Asia courtesy of dovish steer from Lowe \u8226\'20\'22 RBA Governor opened the door to slower rate hikes \u8226\'20\'22 Subsequent climb topped out at 0.6764 (0.6775 was Asia high, pre-Lowe) \u8226\'20\'22 USD may react to comments from Fed chair Powell at 1310 GMT \u8226\'20\'22 Markets currently price 83% chance of another 75 bps Fed hike on Sept 21 \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD bids are tipped around 0.6700 (0.6699 was Tuesday's eight-week low) USD/JPY rise to 150 might tip \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  scales The probability of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordering the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell the dollar against the yen for the first time since 1998 will increase if USD/JPY extends north to 150 rapidly. Japan's deputy chief cabinet secretary \uc2 Seiji Kihara\uc2  on Thursday said Japan was ready to take action to deal with swift yen moves, with Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Masato Kanda saying all options were on the table when he was asked about the chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . USD/JPY soared to a 24-year high just shy of 145 on Wednesday, before a bout of profit-taking on dollar long positions. On Wednesday, Japan's former \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Hiroshi Watanabe told Reuters that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  need not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem yen falls, as such a move would be ineffective in countering broad USD gains. USD/JPY was last at 150 in 1990 (147.64 was the EBS high in 1998). {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3B129Tt"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cede a lot more ground Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been artificially elevated by huge stimulus over the past 14 years and with central banks now rushing to tighten monetary policy, a lot of those gains will be surrendered. Massive stimulus following the global financial crisis in 2008 buoyed emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and they hit record levels on the back of big government spending during the COVID-19 pandemic. Thus their rallies were very extended when the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  signalled a change last year, setting them up for a potentially huge slide. The drop in EM \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  which began when the Fed hiked interest rates in March this year has rattled nerves, forcing a lot of EM central banks to follow the Fed or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation. Yet their falls are relatively small so could extend much further. EM \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are still in the process of unwinding sharp gains resulting from spending during the pandemic, and have a long way to fall to meet the criterion for a minimum technical correction of the rise since 2008. The Fed is far from done with rate hikes while other central banks are just embarking on tightening cycles that will drain the stimulus that was the lifeblood of EM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallies, putting them under much greater pressure. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3D4A5S3"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https: