\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -U.S. dollar rises vs yen as Fed reinforces hawkish stance; euro falls\b0\par\par\uc2 1,005 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2022\par 22:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  hikes rates by 75 basis points\par     * Fed's Powell says Fed needs to keep it going to get job done\par     * Japan ready to take action in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par     * Britain's Queen Elizabeth dies; sterling falls vs dollar\par \par  (Recasts, adds new comment, updates prices)\par     By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par     NEW YORK, Sept 8 (Reuters) - The dollar gained against the yen on Thursday, climbing in nine of the last\par 10 sessions, after Federal Reserve Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2  reiterated that the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue\par to raise interest rates in order to tame surging inflation and warned against prematurely loosening monetary\par policy.\par     For the last several months, dollar-yen has been the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair most sensitive to U.S. rate\par expectations. \par     Across the Atlantic, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  raised interest rates by a record 75 basis points (bps),\par taking the deposit rate above 0% for the first time since 2012. The euro initially went above parity against\par the dollar, but has since weakened amid Powell's comments.\par     Fed officials are soon due to enter a blackout period prior to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Sept. 20-21 meeting.\par     In remarks at a \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cato Institute\f28 \uc2 \f2  conference, Powell said the Fed needs to keep going until it gets the job\par done and is "strongly committed" to bringing inflation down.\par     "I am not convinced that the dollar's highs are in place yet," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marc Chandler\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief market\par strategist, at Bannockburn Global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in New York.\par     "Powell did not add anything new to what he said in Jackson Hole or to what (Fed Vice Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lael)\par Brainard\f28 \uc2 \f2  said yesterday but I expect the dollar to consolidate ahead of CPI (consumer price index) next\par week," he added.\par     U.S. rate futures have priced in an 87% chance the Fed will hike by another 75 bps at this month's\par meeting, which would increase the Fed funds rate to 3.0% to 3.25%.\par     The Fed "could very well do" a 75-bps increase at its September meeting, said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Chicago Fed\f28 \uc2 \f2  President\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Charles Evans\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday, who has tended to be on the dovish side of monetary policy debates.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays\f28 \uc2 \f2 , in its latest research note, said it is also forecasting a 75-bps hike this month, noting it\par sees an outside chance that a softer-than-expected August CPI number will swing the pendulum back toward 50\par bps.\par     In afternoon trading, the dollar rose 0.1% to 143.96 yen. On Tuesday, it surged to a 24-year\par peak of 144.99 yen.\par     The dollar index was flat at 109.63, after soaring to its strongest level since June 2002 the day\par before.\par     The euro, on the other hand, dropped 0.1% to $0.9994.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it expected to continue raising rates to dampen demand, prioritizing the fight against\par inflation.\par     "We have more journey to cover going forward," \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christine Lagarde\f28 \uc2 \f2  told a news conference,\par adding that there had been unanimous agreement about the need for a 75-basis point hike to "frontload" the\par move toward rates.\par     The yen, on the other hand, has been a particular victim of recent dollar strength, as the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par remains the lone dovish \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Japan is ready to take action in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market and will not rule out any options to address\par "clearly excessive volatility" seen in recent yen moves, the country's top \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  diplomat said after a\par meeting between the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Financial Services Agency.\par     Traders are on the lookout for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost the yen.\par     Bannockburn's Chandler believes though that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will unlikely \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market.\par     "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  knows the U.S. is not favor of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Chandler. "Even though (\f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet) Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  doesn't talk about it much, the strong dollar policy is alive and well at the Fed.\par The strong dollar is part of the tightening of financial conditions."\par     In other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , sterling fell against the dollar after Queen Elizabeth, Britain's longest-reigning\par monarch and the nation's figurehead for seven decades, died.\par     \par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid p