\par\par \b \uc2 U.S. dollar rises vs yen as Fed reinforces hawkish stance; euro falls\b0\par\par\uc2 956 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2022\par 22:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Reuters) - The dollar gained against the yen on Thursday, climbing in nine of the last 10 sessions, after Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  reiterated that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to raise interest rates in order to tame surging inflation and warned against prematurely loosening monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 For the last several months, dollar-yen has been the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair most sensitive to U.S. rate expectations.\par \par \uc2 Across the Atlantic, the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates by a record 75 basis points (bps), taking the deposit rate above 0% for the first time since 2012. The euro initially went above parity against the dollar, but has since weakened amid Powell's comments.\par \par \uc2 Fed officials are soon due to enter a blackout period prior to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Sept. 20-21 meeting.\par \par \uc2 In remarks at a \uc2 Cato Institute\uc2  conference, Powell said the Fed needs to keep going until it gets the job done and is "strongly committed" to bringing inflation down. [nL1N30F29H]\par \par \uc2 "I am not convinced that the dollar's highs are in place yet," said \uc2 Marc Chandler\uc2 , chief market strategist, at Bannockburn Global \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "Powell did not add anything new to what he said in Jackson Hole or to what (Fed Vice Chair \uc2 Lael) Brainard\uc2  said yesterday but I expect the dollar to consolidate ahead of CPI (consumer price index) next week," he added.\par \par \uc2 U.S. rate futures have priced in an 87% chance the Fed will hike by another 75 bps at this month's meeting, which would increase the Fed funds rate to 3.0% to 3.25%.\par \par \uc2 The Fed "could very well do" a 75-bps increase at its September meeting, said \uc2 Chicago Fed\uc2  President \uc2 Charles Evans\uc2  on Thursday, who has tended to be on the dovish side of monetary policy debates.\par \par \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , in its latest research note, said it is also forecasting a 75-bps hike this month, noting it sees an outside chance that a softer-than-expected August CPI number will swing the pendulum back toward 50 bps.\par \par \uc2 In afternoon trading, the dollar rose 0.1% to 143.96 yen. On Tuesday, it surged to a 24-year peak of 144.99 yen.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index was flat at 109.63, after soaring to its strongest level since June 2002 the day before.\par \par \uc2 The euro, on the other hand, dropped 0.1% to $0.9994.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ECB\uc2  said it expected to continue raising rates to dampen demand, prioritizing the fight against inflation.\par \par \uc2 "We have more journey to cover going forward," \uc2 ECB\uc2  President \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2  told a news conference, adding that there had been unanimous agreement about the need for a 75-basis point hike to "frontload" the move toward rates.\par \par \uc2 The yen, on the other hand, has been a particular victim of recent dollar strength, as the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  remains the lone dovish \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Japan is ready to take action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will not rule out any options to address "clearly excessive volatility" seen in recent yen moves, the country's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat said after a meeting between the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Financial Services Agency.\par \par \uc2 Traders are on the lookout for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the yen.\par \par \uc2 Bannockburn's Chandler believes though that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will unlikely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  knows the U.S. is not favor of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Chandler. "Even though (\uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  Secretary \uc2 Janet) Yellen\uc2  doesn't talk about it much, the strong dollar policy is alive and well at the Fed. The strong dollar is part of the tightening of financial conditions."\par \par \uc2 In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , sterling fell against the dollar after Queen Elizabeth, Britain's longest-reigning monarch and the nation's figurehead for seven decades, died. [GBP/]\par \par \uc2 ========================================================\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 3:51PM (1951 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Description RIC Last U.S. Close Pct Change YTD Pct High Bid Low Bid\par \par \uc2 Previous Change\par \par \uc2 Session\par \par \uc2 Dollar index 109.6400 109.6900 -0.04% 14.611% +110.2500 +109.3300\par \par \uc2 Euro/Dollar $0.9997 $1.0008 -0.10% -12.06% +$1.0030 +$0.9931\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Yen 143.9700 143.7700 +0.14% +25.06% +144.5500 +143.3250\par \par \uc2 Euro/Yen 143.92 143.85 +0.05% +10.44% +144.3000 +143.1900\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Swiss 0.9709 0.9764 -0.55% +6.45% +0.9782 +0.9707\par \par \uc2 Sterling/Dollar $1.1499 $1.1535 -0.30% -14.97% +$1.1560 +$1.1464\par \par \uc2 Dollar/Canadian 1.3092 1.3119 -0.19% +3.56% +1.3159 +1.3078\par \par \uc2 Aussie/Dollar $0.6749 $0.6769 -0.28% -7.15% +$0.6774 +$0.6713\par \par \uc2 Euro/Swiss 0.9704 0.9768 -0.66% -6.41% +0.9777 +0.9662\par \par \uc2 Euro/Sterling 0.8692 0.8673 +0.22% +3.48% +0.8712 +0.8655\par \par \uc2 NZ $0.6051 $0.6074 -0.37% -11.59% +$0.6078 +$0.6033\par \par \uc2 Do