\par\par \b \uc2 EXPLAINER-What would  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  to shore up the weak yen look like?\b0\par\par\uc2 675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 September 2022\par 12:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with new top, additional information on 'rate checks')\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara and Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 Sept 8 - Japan is ready to take action to address "clearly excessive volatility" seen in the yen, the country's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat said on Thursday, issuing the strongest warning to date after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunged to 24-year lows.\par \par \uc2 Aside from verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has several options to stem excessive yen falls. Among them is to directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling dollars and buying up large amounts of yen.\par \par \uc2 The precipitous slide in Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has run so far and fast it's spooking big investors, and some are already cutting bets that it will decline further, anticipating policymakers may soon step in to try and arrest the freefall.\par \par \uc2 Below are details on how yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could work, the likelihood of this happening as well as challenges:\par \par \uc2 WHEN DID \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  LAST CONDUCT YEN-BUYING \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 Given the economy's heavy reliance on exports, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has historically focused on arresting sharp yen rises and taken a hands-off approach on yen falls.\par \par \uc2 Yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been very rare. The last time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in 1998, when the Asian financial crisis triggered a yen sell-off and a rapid capital outflow from the region. Before that, Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter yen falls in 1991-1992.\par \par \uc2 WHAT WOULD PROMPT TOKYO TO BUY YEN AGAIN?\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is costly and could easily fail given the difficulty of influencing its value in the huge global \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 That is one key reason it is considered a last-resort move, which Tokyo would greenlight only when verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fails to prevent a free fall in the yen. The speed of yen declines, not just levels, would be crucial in authorities' decision on whether and when to step in.\par \par \uc2 Some policymakers say \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would only become an option if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  faces a "triple" threat -- selling of yen, domestic stocks and bonds -- in what would be similar to sharp capital outflows experienced in some emerging economies.\par \par \uc2 WHAT COME NEXT AFTER VERBAL WARNINGS?\par \par \uc2 Before directly stepping into the market, Japanese authorities traditionally conduct "rate checks," a practice where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials call up dealers asking for the price of buying or selling yen.\par \par \uc2 The move will be a strong sign that actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is close. Authorities will take such steps in hope that the move alone would scare market players enough to influence yen moves to their favour.\par \par \uc2 HOW WOULD ACTUAL \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WORK?\par \par \uc2 When \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen rises, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  issues short-term bills to raise yen which it can then sell in the market to weaken the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value.\par \par \uc2 If it were to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop yen falls, authorities must tap \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves for dollars to sell in the market in exchange for yen.\par \par \uc2 In both cases, the finance minister will issue the final order to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will act as an agent and execute the order in the market.\par \par \uc2 WHAT ARE THE CHALLENGES?\par \par \uc2 Yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more difficult than yen-selling.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves stand at $1.33 trillion, the world's second largest after China's and likely comprised mostly of dollars. While abundant, reserves could quickly dwindle if huge sums are required to influence rates each time Tokyo steps in.\par \par \uc2 That means there are limits to how long it can keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , unlike for yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - where Tokyo can continue issuing bills to raise yen.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would also require informal consent by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's G7 counterparts, notably the United States if it were to be conducted against the dollar/yen. That is not easy with Washington traditionally opposed to the idea of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , except in cases of extreme market volatility. (Reporting by Leika Kihara and Tetsushi Kajimoto Editing by Vidya Ranganathan and Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-8T11:54:34.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220908ei9801xdb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
