 "concerned" \u8226\'20\'22 King dollar stomps on yen as U.S. yields rise \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY soars to 144.44 on Wednesday, on the EBS prices, a new 24-year high \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY chart remains very bullish, expect even bigger gains \u8226\'20\'22 Japan stocks fall despite exporters' boost from plummeting yen \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/JPY usually makes gains in September \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/JPY's correlation with USD/JPY high, 30/60-day logs are above +0.50 GBP/USD holds near 30-month low as \uc2 BoE\uc2  quartet speak to MPs \u8226\'20\'22 Cable trades below 1.15 as four BoE MPC members speak to MPs on UK TSC \u8226\'20\'22 BoE says Truss energy plans could slow inflation \u8226\'20\'22 Truss energy announcement expected Thursday (week before \uc2 BoE\uc2  rate decision) \u8226\'20\'22 1.1444 was 30-month low for GBP/USD earlier this week \u8226\'20\'22 1.1413 was 35-year low in March 2020 (1.0075 mooted as record low in 1985) \u8226\'20\'22 Murmors of 'sterling crisis' no longer fanciful AUD/USD holds close to 8-week low before \uc2 RBA\uc2  chief speaks \u8226\'20\'22 0.6733 is AUD/USD high water-mark since its 0.6699 eight-week low in Asia \u8226\'20\'22 That low was plumbed as USD index scaled new 20-year peak \u8226\'20\'22 0.6683 (July 14, two-year low) and 0.6650 are support points below 0.6699 \u8226\'20\'22 \uc2 RBA\uc2 's Lowe to speak about "Inflation and Monetary Policy Framework" Thursday \u8226\'20\'22 Lowe speech at 1.05pm AEST. \uc2 RBA\uc2  raised rates by 50 bps Tuesday \u8226\'20\'22 Next Fed rate decision Sept 21: 72% chance of 75 bps hike Japan's yen, weak by design, should continue to fall For years Japan's yen has been weighed by Japanese policies, and unless they change it should continue to fall. Its \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly affirmed its commitment to super-easy monetary policy with a pledge to buy unlimited numbers of bonds if required. With the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  significantly tightening policy this year, USD/JPY has soared, triggering a rather surprising reaction about the one-side nature of the move in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . While this has spurred speculation about potential \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb USD/JPY's rise, that seems unlikely unless Japan intends to end the policies that have brought yen down. On a trade-weighted basis, the yen is close to a 50-year low. It has been falling since 1995, fuelled by increasingly easy policies yet inflation has still taken two decades to return to target. To abandon the policies that helped achieve that goal a few months after the fact seems as unlikely as a unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem a USD/JPY rise that brings the pair into line with what yen has been doing more broadly for years. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3KUAyI9"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3AWm6uF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  Houston, without YCC change, Japan has an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  problem Actions speak louder than words, so if Tokyo really wants to turn the USD/JPY tide it may need the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  to ditch its commitment to capping the yield on the 10-year government bond at 0.25%. The cap has resulted in the yield spread of the 10-year \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  bond over its Japanese counterpart ballooning as UST yields jump. That has propelled USD/JPY to a 24-year EBS high of 144.38, prompting Japanese concern about "rapid, one-sided" moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The higher that USD/JPY goes, the greater the chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  ordering the BoJ to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell the dollar against the yen - something it last did in June 1998, when USD/JPY was above 146. The USD/JPY surge comes after IMM speculators last month reduced their net JPY short position to the lowest since March 2021. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3cWiTDp"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here}}}\uc2  To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-10T11:00:43.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220907ei97025p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
