\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Resilient U.S. dollar soars to 24-year high vs yen, 37-year peak vs sterling\b0\par\par\uc2 1,019 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2022\par 21:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  hikes rates by 75 bps\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  seen raising rates by 75 bps as well \par     * Chinese yuan sinks to two-year low vs dollar\par     * Bitcoin falls to lowest since June, but last trading higher\par \par  (Adds new comments, updates prices)\par     By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par     NEW YORK, Sept 7 (Reuters) - The dollar surged to a 24-year peak against the yen and a 37-year high\par versus sterling on Wednesday, as Japan's dovish monetary policy and Europe's economic problems contrasted\par with a relatively stronger U.S. economy and a hawkish \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  determined to bring down inflation to\par its 2% inflation target.\par     The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  soared as high as 144.99 yen, hitting the level for the first time since\par August 1998. It is now within a large leap of its 1998 high of 147.43. The dollar was last up 0.9% at 144.09\par yen.\par     Against sterling, the greenback hit $1.1407, the lowest since 1985 and last down 0.1% at\par $1.1509. \par     "Increasingly, it is becoming a growth story and really a crisis story. We have China continuing to have\par a COVID-zero policy, and if anything continuing to double down, locking down more cities," said Erik Nelson,\par macro strategist, at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Wells Fargo\f28 \uc2 \f2  in New York City.\par     "Europe and the UK look like they are headed for a challenging couple of months, with recession very\par likely for both economies. The U.S., on the other hand, looks resilient," he added.\par     The euro fell below 99 cents on Wednesday after dipping as low as $0.9864 on Tuesday, its\par lowest since October 2002. Europe's single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was last up 0.8% at US$0.9985.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is seen likely to deliver a massive 75 basis-point (bp) rate hike on Thursday,\par but these expectations have done little to support the euro given a battered European economy and Russia's\par decision to keep the key Nord Stream 1 gas pipeline shut indefinitely.\par     In contrast, a report overnight showed the U.S. services industry unexpectedly picked up last month,\par underpinning the view that the economy is not in recession.\par     Also on Wednesday, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  raised interest rates by 75 bps to a 14-year high on Wednesday, as\par expected, and said the policy rate would need to go even higher as it battles raging inflation.\par     Despite the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BoC\f28 \uc2 \f2  rate hike, the U.S. dollar was little changed against the Canadian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at C$1.3141\par .\par     Moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets were most dramatic on the yen, whose tumble, even by its own recent standards,\par has been precipitous. Since the beginning of August, the yen has plummeted by 10.1% against the dollar\par .\par     At current dollar/yen levels, speculation is also growing that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prop up the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Every time the yen weakens, it asks the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BOJ\f28 \uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) a question, as to whether now is the time\par to abandon YCC (yield curve control)?," wrote \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alan Ruskin\f28 \uc2 \f2 , macro strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in its latest\par research note.\par     "When nothing more than verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is at hand, the market can read from the lip service that\par the authorities are still some way from tightening monetary policy." \par     Japan's Chief Cabinet Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hirokazu Matsuno\f28 \uc2 \f2  told a news briefing that the administration would like\par to take necessary steps if "rapid, one-sided" moves in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets continue, ratcheting up the\par rhetoric. \par     However, many analysts see \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as difficult given that global central banks are more focused on\par inflation rather than exchange rates.\par     Elsewhere China's yuan sank to a two-year trough, closing in on the 7-per-dollar mark despite steps by\par authorities to stem its decline. The onshore yuan weakened to a low of 6.9808, the lowest since\par August 2020, and the offshore yuan was even closer to the key level, falling as low as 6.997 per\par dollar.\par     Cryptocurrency bitcoin earlier slumped to the lowest since June 19 at $18,540, extending a 5%\par tumble from Tuesday. It was last up 1.6% at $19,078.\par     \par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 3:14PM (1914 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct       High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                   \par                                               Session                                             \par  Dollar index                 109.7300       110.3400    -0.55%         14.705%       +110.7900   +109