\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -U.S. dollar soars to 24-year high vs yen, 37-year peak vs sterling\b0\par\par\uc2 1,021 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2022\par 16:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  hikes rates by 75 bps\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  seen raising rates by 75 bps as well \par     * Chinese yuan sinks to two-year low vs dollar\par     * Bitcoin falls to lowest since June but last trading higher\par \par  (Adds new comment, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  table, byline, NEW YORK dateline; updates prices)\par     By Alun John and Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par     LONDON/NEW YORK, Sept 7 (Reuters) - The dollar surged to a 24-year peak against the yen and a 37-year\par high versus sterling as Japan's dovish monetary policy and Europe's economic problems contrasted with a\par relatively stronger U.S. economy and a hawkish \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  determined to bring down inflation to its 2%\par inflation target.\par     The U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  soared as high as 144.99 yen, hitting the level for the first time since\par August 1998. It is now within a large leap of its 1998 high of 147.43. The dollar was last up 1.1% at\par 144.305 yen.\par     "The dollar is a rock in a sea of troubles right now, outperforming all of its major rivals as interest\par rates rise and the economy shows signs of resilience," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Karl Schamotta\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chief market strategist, at\par Corpay in Toronto.\par     "With measures of core inflation barely budging, and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (BoJ) showing no inclination to\par change direction, yield differentials have continued to worsen - depressing returns in relative terms and\par adding fuel to a burgeoning yen-funded carry trade," he said.\par     In carry trades, investors borrow in low-yielding \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  such as the yen or Swiss franc to purchase\par higher-yielding ones such as the Australian or New Zealand dollars.\par     Against sterling, the greenback hit $1.1407, the lowest since 1985 and last down 0.8% at\par $1.1425. \par     The euro fell below 99 cents on Wednesday after dipping as low as $0.9864 on Tuesday, its\par lowest since October 2002. Europe's single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was last up 0.3% at US$0.9930.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is seen as more likely than not to deliver a massive 75 basis-point (bp) rate\par hike on Thursday, but these expectations are doing little to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the face of a battered\par European economy and Russia's decision to keep the key Nord Stream 1 gas pipeline shut indefinitely.\par \par     In contrast, a report overnight showed the U.S. services industry unexpectedly picked up last month,\par supporting the view that the economy is not in recession.\par     Also on Wednesday, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  hiked interest rates by 75 bps three-quarters of a percentage\par point to a 14-year high on Wednesday, as expected, and said the policy rate would need to go even higher as\par it battles raging inflation.\par     Despite the \f28 \uc2 \f2 BoC\f28 \uc2 \f2  rate hike, the U.S. dollar was steady against the Canadian  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , up 0.1% at\par C$1.3164.\par     Moves in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets were most dramatic for the yen, whose tumble, even by its own recent standards,\par has been precipitous. The dollar has climbed 4.2% from 138.96 yen just since the end of August. \par     At the current dollar/yen levels, speculation is also growing that Japanese authorities could \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to prop up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Chief Cabinet Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hirokazu Matsuno\f28 \uc2 \f2  told a news briefing that the administration would like\par to take necessary steps if "rapid, one-sided" moves in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets continue, ratcheting up the\par rhetoric. \par     However, many analysts see \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as difficult. \par     "Foreign central banks are prioritising dealing with inflation, and cannot afford to worry about\par exchange rate fluctuations," said Rikiya Takebe, senior strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Okasan Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par      Elsewhere China's yuan sank to a two-year trough, closing in on the 7-per-dollar mark despite steps by\par authorities to stem its decline. \par     The onshore yuan weakened to a low of 6.9808, the softest level since August 2020, and the\par offshore yuan was even closer to the key level, falling as low as 6.997 per dollar.\par     Cryptocurrency bitcoin slumped to the lowest since June 19 at $18,540, extending a 5% tumble\par from Tuesday. But it was last up 0.7% at $18,920.\par     \par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 10:42AM (1442 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct       High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                   \par                                               Session                        