\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -King dollar stomps on yen, sterling under heavy pressure\b0\par\par\uc2 619 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2022\par 14:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO/LONDON, Sept 7 (Reuters) - The dollar was lord of all it surveyed on Wednesday, at a fresh 24-year peak on the rate-sensitive yen and retesting multi year highs on the euro and sterling as economic problems in Europe contrasted with a strong U.S. economy.\par \par \uc2 The dollar soared as high as 144.99 yen , up 1.5%, hitting the level for the first time since August 1998. It is now within a large leap of its 1998 high of 147.43.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile sterling was at $1.4175, down 0.7%. It was holding just above the $1.1413 level, a fall below which would be its weakest level since 1985, according to Refinitiv data.\par \par \uc2 The euro wallowed below 99 cents after dipping as low as $0.9864 overnight, its lowest since late 2002.\par \par \uc2 "So far this week its been a dollar move being driven by rising economic hard landing risks in Europe, and the back-up in various forms of European risk premia related to the fiscal picture, stagflation, and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightening into what is likely to be a recession," said \uc2 Stephen Gallo\uc2 , European head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 BMO Capital Markets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The only question on the recession is how deep and protracted."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen as more likely than not to deliver a massive 75 bps rate hike on Thursday, but these expectations are doing little to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the face of a battered European economy and Russia's decision to keep the key Nord Stream 1 gas pipeline shut indefinitely.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, a report overnight showed the U.S. services industry unexpectedly picked up last month, supporting the view that the economy is not in recession and giving the Fed leeway for another 75-basis-point rate rise on Sept. 21.\par \par \uc2 But the moves were most dramatic for the yen, whose tumble, even by its own recent standards, has been precipitous. The dollar has climbed 4.2% from 138.96 yen just since the end of August.\par \par \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is extremely sensitive to moves in long-term U.S. interest rates, and the yield on the 10-year Treasury note climbed as high as 3.365% in Tokyo trading, a level not seen since June 16, before retreating a little.\par \par \uc2 At these levels, speculation is also growing that Japanese authorities could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top government spokesperson, Chief Cabinet Secretary \uc2 Hirokazu Matsuno\uc2 , told a news briefing that the administration would like to take necessary steps if "rapid, one-sided" moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets continue, ratcheting up the rhetoric.\par \par \uc2 However, many analysts see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as difficult.\par \par \uc2 "Foreign central banks are prioritising dealing with inflation, and cannot afford to worry about exchange rate fluctuations," said Rikiya Takebe, senior strategist at \uc2 Okasan Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or policy revisions by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to be difficult, and it will not be easy to stop the yen from falling."\par \par \uc2 Elsewhere China's yuan sank to a two-year trough, closing in on the 7-per-dollar mark despite steps by authorities to stem its decline.\par \par \uc2 The onshore yuan weakened to a low of 6.9808, the softest level since August 2020, and the offshore yuan was even closer to the key level, falling as low as 6.997 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency bitcoin slumped to the lowest since June 19 at $18,540, extending a 5% tumble from Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Buckland in Tokyo, Tom Westbrook in Singapore, and Alun John in London; Additional reporting by Daiki Iga; Editing by Kim Coghill, Bradley Perrett and Chizu Nomiyama) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-7T13:47:38.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220907ei9702noh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
