\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -King dollar crushes yen as aggressive Fed bets ramp up\b0\par\par\uc2 719 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 September 2022\par 07:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 7 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a 24-year high against the yen on Wednesday after U.S. economic data reinforced the view that the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  will continue aggressive policy tightening.\par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan sank to a two-year trough, closing in on the psychologically important 7 per dollar mark despite steps by authorities to stem its decline. The Philippine peso slid to a record low.\par \par \uc2 The euro languished not far from Tuesday's two-decade low, well below parity, as \uc2 European Union\uc2  ministers prepare to meet on Friday to discuss the energy crisis that is hammering industry and squeezing households.\par \par \uc2 A report overnight showed the U.S. services industry unexpectedly picked up last month, reinforcing the view that the economy is not in recession and giving the Fed leeway for another super-sized 75 basis-point rate rise on Sept. 21.\par \par \uc2 Markets currently give that scenario 75% probability, with 25% odds for a half-point hike.\par \par \uc2 The dollar soared as high as 144.38 yen for the first time since August 1998. Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is extremely sensitive to moves in long-term U.S. rates, and the yield on the 10-year Treasury note climbed as high as 3.365% in Tokyo trading, a level not seen since June 16.\par \par \uc2 Japan's top government spokesperson, Chief Cabinet Secretary \uc2 Hirokazu Matsuno\uc2 , told a news briefing that the administration would like to take necessary steps if "rapid, one-sided" moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets continue, ratcheting up the rhetoric to describe the yen's nearly 9% month-long decline.\par \par \uc2 Earlier in the day, Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  was quoted using the same language by Jiji news agency.\par \par \uc2 "The speed at which the dollar is appreciating against the yen is getting out of control and is at risk of becoming unanchored," said Davis Hall, head of capital markets at Indosuez Wealth Management Asia.\par \par \uc2 "Right now you're drawing in everybody to stop out by throwing in the towel," he said. "We could reach 148 without MOF (\b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) action."\par \par \uc2 However, many analysts see \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as difficult with the momentum behind the yen's decline against the dollar driven by a widening divergence in monetary policy. Unilateral action would be even less effective, they say.\par \par \uc2 "Foreign central banks are prioritizing dealing with inflation, and cannot afford to worry about exchange rate fluctuations," said Rikiya Takebe, senior strategist at \uc2 Okasan Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  or policy revisions by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely to be difficult, and it will not be easy to stop the yen from falling."\par \par \uc2 The dollar will remain a force to reckon with over the remainder of this year and into the next as U.S. interest rates rise and the economy outperforms its peers, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists in a Reuters poll.\par \par \uc2 The euro wallowed below 99 cents, after dipping as low as $0.9864 overnight.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen likely to deliver a 75 bps rate hike on Thursday, but traders seem more focused on Russia's decision to keep the key Nord Stream 1 gas pipeline shut indefinitely.\par \par \uc2 Sterling shed 0.32% to $1.1480, approaching the 2 1/2-year low of $1.1444 reached on Monday, with Britain also entangled in the energy crisis, despite new prime minister \uc2 Liz Truss\uc2 's plans for a massive support package.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar index, which measures the greenback against six major peers, hit a fresh 20-year high of 110.69.\par \par \uc2 The onshore yuan weakened to a low of 6.9808, the softest level since August 2020, even after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued to set the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's official guidance firmer than market forecasts. Disappointing Chinese trade data further dented sentiment.\par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso sank to a record-low 57.32 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar dropped to the lowest since May 2020 at $0.5997, and the Singapore dollar declined to the weakest since June 2020 at 1.4107 per greenback.\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency bitcoin slumped to the lowest since June 19 at $18,540, extending a 5% tumble from Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kevin Buckland and Tom Westbrook; Additional reporting by Daiki Iga; Editing by Ana Nicolaci da Costa and Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-9-7T06:24:24.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220907ei9700rut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
