\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Yen hits lowest exchange rate against the dollar since 1998\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 September 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The yen plummeted on Thursday (1) to a 24-year low against the dollar, which benefited from its status as a security asset in an altered market and also advanced against the euro and the British pound.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which furthermore suffers from a rather accommodative policy of the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (BoJ, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), was quoted at 140 yen per dollar Thursday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 The devaluation of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has lost more than 20% in a year, is due, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders, to the very flexible monetary policy of the BoJ.\par \par \uc2 Unlike in the United States and Europe, where inflation has soared and even exceeded 10% in the UK, Japan's price increase was 2.4% over the past 12 months in July, a rate very close to the 2% target of major central banks, which has led the BoJ to a situation of passivity.\par \par \uc2 Previously, when the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy yen, it was around these levels," David Forrester, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Cr\u233\'00\'E9dit Agricole in Hong Kong, told AFP.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's passivity contrasts with the firm stance of the \uc2 US Federal Reserve\uc2  (Fed, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), which has signaled on several occasions that it will continue to raise interest rates to fight inflation.\par \par \uc2 "Last week's comments by Fed Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , who promised to act quickly to control inflation without worrying about the effects of this on the U.S. economy," benefit the dollar, analysts at financial services firm \uc2 OFX\uc2  opine.\par \par \uc2 Thus, the performance of other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar was not much better either: the euro was quoted at $0.99 and the British pound at $1.15 on Thursday afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220901ei9100ixa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
