\par\par \b \uc2 Yen to remain weaker than key 130-per-dollar level at year-end - Reuters poll\b0\par\par\uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2022\par 02:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Reuters) - The Japanese yen will likely remain weaker than the key psychological level of 130 per dollar over the next six months as a gap between Japanese and U.S. benchmark yields weighs on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a Reuters poll showed.\par \par \uc2 This year the yen has slumped against the greenback and other major peers as the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (\uc2 BOJ\uc2 ) resolutely stuck to its ultra-dovish monetary policy, in contrast to a growing number of increasingly hawkish central banks overseas.\par \par \uc2 Weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes mainly from widening interest rate differentials between Japan and elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 In the July 1-6 poll, the median forecast was for Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen to 131 per dollar in six months' time, compared with 126.84 in last month's forecast, meaning it would stay weaker than the 130-yen-per-dollar level.\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its weakest against the dollar since 1998 at 137 last week.\par \par \uc2 Seven of 61 respondents projected the yen to be at a weaker level than that six months from now, including four forecasting it to be at 140.\par \par \uc2 Despite the yen's rapid decline this year - it has lost about 15% against the greenback - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stop it from sliding, 45% of 22 poll respondents said.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  will probably be forced to abandon the yield curve control policy in the coming months if JPY depreciates further. However, direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks unlikely," said Roberto Cobo Garcia, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 BBVA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some market players have speculated the country could conduct yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest sharp falls in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after authorities stepped up their warnings about its strong declines.\par \par \uc2 While the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  has firmly rejected the idea of adjusting its policy in the face of the yen's falls, some strategists said it would be the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , not the government, that would move first if policymakers were to act in response to its declines.\par \par \uc2 "Japanese officials have been expressing concerns over yen weakness, and the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  highlighted that a rapid depreciation of the yen has a negative impact on the economy," said Khoon Goh, head of Asia research at \uc2 ANZ Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "At this stage, JPY weakness is not enough for the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  to change its monetary policy stance, but if there is a push towards 140-150, the situation could change."\par \par \uc2 Ten of 22 poll respondents said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That compared with six respondents who predicted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the 140 yen per dollar level, and four who chose 145 as the likely trigger level. One selected 150 as the dollar/yen rate at which \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while another said 155 or weaker.\par \par \uc2 The last time the authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the yen was in 1998.\par \par \uc2 (For other stories from the July Reuters \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  poll:)\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Vivek Mishra in Bengaluru; Polling by Sujith Pai, Aditi Verma and Sarupya Ganguly; Editing by Ross Finley) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-7-7T00:11:21.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220707ei77000m9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
