\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Japan's Kanda reappointed as top  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  diplomat amid markets jitters\b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2022\par 03:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, background)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 17 (Reuters) - Japan has reappointed Masato Kanda as vice finance minister for international affairs, the country's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat, as part of a mid-year personnel reshuffle, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The government wants to stabilise financial markets as the yen hits 24-year lows - beyond 135 to the dollar - this week and rising bond yields heap pressure on the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yield curve control.\par \par \uc2 Kanda would oversee \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent excess volatility from hurting economic and financial stability, amid speculation that Tokyo may sell the dollar to buy yen.\par \par \uc2 Under Kanda, Japan would host gatherings of financial leaders from the \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  advanced nations next year in the run-up to the \uc2 G7\uc2  leaders' summit.\par \par \uc2 Kanda is also tasked with coordinating with the broader G20 finance chiefs to respond to the COVID-19 pandemic, and tackle global tax and emerging-market debt.\par \par \uc2 The appointment will take effect June 24 after approval from Prime Minister \uc2 Fumio Kishida\uc2 's cabinet.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not conducted dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to back the yen since 1998 and it has stayed out of the market since the aftermath of the 2011 earthquake and nuclear crisis.\par \par \uc2 Kanda is known for his broad international experience and close ties with policymakers, having worked with the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  as deputy vice minister for policy planning and coordination.\par \par \uc2 Kanda is close to \uc2 BOJ\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2 , who was vice finance minister for international affairs for 3-1/2 years to January 2003. Both Kanda and Kuroda graduated from the prestigious \uc2 University of Tokyo\uc2  and studied at the \uc2 University of Oxford\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The government's annual reshuffle also named Eiji Chatani as administrative vice finance minister - the top bureaucrat at the finance ministry - to replace Koji Yano, the ministry said. (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto; editing by Richard Pullin and Gerry Doyle) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-6-17T02:06:58.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220617ei6h0028l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
