\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Falling yen is negative for the economy, says \uc2 BoJ\b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (BoJ) President \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  said Monday that sharp falls in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are negative and undesirable ??for the economy as they cloud the outlook and increase uncertainty for companies in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 "Recent sharp falls in the yen are increasing uncertainty about the outlook and making it difficult for companies to compile business plans, so they are negative and undesirable ??for the economy," Kuroda said.\par \par \uc2 "It is important that companies that have seen their profits improve due to the yen devaluation increase capital spending and wages, and a positive cycle of more income and spending will emerge for the economy," the BoJ chief said.\par \par \uc2 Kuroda's remarks were made as the yen fell to a 23-year low against the dollar earlier in the day, rocking the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets.\par \par \uc2 In the recent past, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had no problem unilaterally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when it feels the yen is unduly low against its major peers, a point made clear by Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  on Monday.\par \par \uc2 While choosing not to refer to any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to balance the equation, Suzuki said during a parliamentary session that he sees "more of the downside of yen weakness emerging."\par \par \uc2 "Even if the yen depreciates and import costs rise, it wouldn't be a problem as long as wages grow to offset the impact. But right now, wage growth is weak, so I see more of the downside of yen weakness emerging," Suzuki added.\par \par \uc2 Kuroda, meanwhile, said that the BoJ, in close coordination with the Finance Ministry, will continue to monitor developments in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and how sudden fluctuations may affect the economy and prices. He reiterated the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's firm stance that it will continue its over-easy monetary easing amid skyrocketing commodity prices and commodity costs in resource-poor Japan, which are piling inflationary pressure on the economy.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Central Banks in the US and Europe have been aggressively tightening their monetary policies and raising interest rates to combat skyrocketing inflation, meaning that the interest rate gap between Japan and some other major economies has widened rapidly and is possibly set to widen further.\par \par \uc2 Xinhua Agency\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220615ei6f008h0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
