\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The yen activates the time machine and returns to 1998: what does it mean for investors?\b0\par\par\uc2 863 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The yen has traveled in the time machine to land in 1998. This week, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at a 24-year low against the dollar, although on Wednesday it recorded a timid rebound that takes it somewhat away from those lows. This disparity has been accentuated by the weakness of this \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and by the strengthening of the dollar, which is at its highest level since 2002.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan has been reluctant to raise interest rates. On the contrary, the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  has hardly hesitated to activate rate hikes in order to curb the high levels of inflation in the United States.\par \par \uc2 The yen is the world's third most traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and represents the world's fourth largest economy. The weakness is due to the widening gap between interest spreads on Japanese debt and those of the rest of the world. In fact, this trend has been accentuated in recent weeks, with even the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  setting the tone for a rate hike. The same is not true of the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , which has increased its accommodative monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 How to put an end to this situation?\par \par \uc2 Improved growth prospects with the reopening of borders after Covid-19 and high inflation are the reasons that may lead the Japanese supervisor to reverse its dovish monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Consumer prices in the country marked 2.1% in April, one tenth above the inflation target set by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 . This is the first time this barrier has been exceeded in seven years. This, if anything, comes as more of a surprise to analysts in a country that has been battling deflation for decades. "The fall of the yen can stop if the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  changes course and becomes aggressive," stresses Francesca Fornasari, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  solutions at Insight Investments, in statements reported by Reuters.\par \par \uc2 For now, however, the Japanese financial authorities have yet to make a statement in favor of such a change. The last time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in 1998, following the strong capital outflows caused by the Asian financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Weak yen, good or bad for the economy?\par \par \uc2 The yen has weakened to near 7-year lows against the Chinese yuan. A similar situation is occurring in the cross with the Korean won and the Taiwanese dollar. This is a relief for a balance of trade deficit.\par \par \uc2 The weakness of the yen has also boosted the attractiveness of the Japanese stock market. Many international investors now consider Japanese indices to be undervalued against European and U.S. financial markets.\par \par \uc2 "Analyzing the Japanese market internally, we see that the valuation-to-earnings ratios (P/E) of small companies were not lower (cheaper) than that of large companies since 2012-2013. Throughout 2021 and 2022 they are already trading at a discount again, a very unusual aspect that reflects the current opportunity in this segment," the Japan Deep Value fund managers assess in their latest quarterly letter.\par \par \uc2 Rising rates in other geographies have the opposite effect for Japanese investors. The weakness of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  puts them in a bind: yields are high and rising, making foreign bonds more attractive.\par \par \uc2 An investment opportunity?\par \par \uc2 The Japanese stock market is one of the worst performers for investors this year. However, the devaluation of the Nikkei 225, its largest stock index, opens up opportunities for individuals. Companies such as \uc2 Mitsubishi\uc2 , Honda, \uc2 Toyota\uc2 , \uc2 Canon\uc2 , \uc2 Sony\uc2  and \uc2 Fujitsu\uc2  are part of this index and now have more attractive valuations than in the past due to the falls in the index.\par \par \uc2 One way of taking a position in listed companies in Japan, apart from the direct purchase of shares, is to invest in mutual funds. There are funds that invest in the Asia-Pacific region and give a significant weighting to the Japanese country in their portfolio. This is the case of Allianz Oriental Income, from the German fund manager \uc2 Allianz Global Investors\uc2 . One fifth of the portfolio is invested in Japanese companies such as \uc2 Toyota\uc2 . The portfolio is completed with exposure to stocks from other countries and territories in the region, such as Taiwan, China, Australia and New Zealand.\par \par \uc2 Investors who want to directly capture the appreciation potential of the Japanese market have investment vehicles with pure exposure. One option piloted by a Spanish entity is Ibercaja Japan, an Ibercaja Gesti\u243\'00\'F3n fund that invests its clients' assets in large-cap equities. In other words, a portfolio composed of large Japanese listed companies in sectors such as technology (e.g. the semiconductor company \uc2 Tokyo Electron\uc2 ), health (the medical device manufacturer Terumo) or cyclical consumption (\uc2 Fast Retailing\uc2 , parent company of Uniqlo).\par \par \uc2 Another option is the Japan Deep Value fund, an actively managed financial product focused on small- and mid-cap companies. It achieves an annualized return of 4% over the last 3 years. With this product, the investor purchases a portfolio with holdings in mainly Japanese industrial and technology firms. Users can also consult an investment showcase in Asia through Finect.\par \par \uc2 How much can I earn by investing for the long term?\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220615ei6f005l3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
