\par\par \b \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  sees dollar topping 140 yen as policy diverges more\b0\par\par\uc2 442 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2022\par 10:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 15 (Reuters) - The U.S. dollar will soon rise above 140 yen as the Federal Reserve possibly gets even more hawkish on rates while the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  digs in its heels on ultra-easy policy, according to a forecast by \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  strategists.\par \par \uc2 The dollar reached the highest since October 1998 at 135.60 yen on Wednesday, with markets now expecting the Fed to tighten policy by 75 basis points at a meeting later in the day and again next month, a scale of moves not seen since 1984.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  has restated his commitment to massive stimulus several times this month ahead of a policy decision on Friday, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has ramped up bond purchase \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week to keep long-term yields close to the zero policy rate.\par \par \uc2 "Assuming \uc2 BOJ\uc2  inaction and a hawkish Fed outcome, USD/JPY should be able to extend its rise toward the 140 handle over the near-term horizon, and our bias on the pair remains skewed higher," \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  strategists Benjamin Shatil and Sosuke Nakamura wrote in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 The dollar is already trading at a 2-3 yen discount to where it should be based on yield differentials, "which have been the single most important driver of the pair over the past year," because of the risk premium ahead of those two big events, they wrote, meaning it could snap higher on as-expected outcomes.\par \par \uc2 They also called the risk of full-blown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  "overstated," even though yen weakness had exacerbated price rises in gasoline and food before crucial upper house elections next month, because the catalyst had been the divergence in monetary policy rather than speculative bets.\par \par \uc2 "It is simply not a credible proposition to argue that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can halt the yen's slide," they wrote.\par \par \uc2 The real risk to yen short positions came from the potential for the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's capitulation on its ultra-easy policy, they said.\par \par \uc2 Speculators are challenging the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve to its yield curve control policy that pins the 10-year at zero by targeting futures and seven-year cash bonds, pushing them to multi-year extremes on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  strategists said the baseline view was that this week's meeting would be too soon for such a shift, but that eventual "surrender" on YCC would trigger a spike in yields that in turn could lead to a 3-4% correction lower for the dollar-yen rate. (Reporting by Kevin Buckland; Editing by Edmund Blair) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-6-15T09:42:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220615ei6f01d89\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
