:30 US May Core CPI Index SA, 290.46 prev \u8226\'20\'22 12:30 US May CPI MM SA, 0.7% f'cast, 0.3% prev \u8226\'20\'22 12:30 US May CPI MM NSA, 0.560% prev; YY NSA, 8.3% f'cast, 8.3% prev \u8226\'20\'22 12:30 CA May Employment Change, 30.0k f'cast, 15.3k prev \u8226\'20\'22 12:30 CA May Unemployment Rate, 5.2% f'cast, 5.2% prev \u8226\'20\'22 12:30 CA May Full Time Employment Change, -31.6k prev; Part Time, 47.1k prev \u8226\'20\'22 14:00 US Jun U Mich Sentiment Prelim, 58.0 f'cast, 58.4 prev \u8226\'20\'22 14:00 US Jun U Mich Conditions Prelim, 62.5 f'cast, 63.3 prev; Expectations, 54.5 f'cast, 55.2 prev \u8226\'20\'22 14:00 US Jun U Mich 1Yr Inf Prelim, 5.3% prev; 5-Yr, 3.0% prev \u8226\'20\'22 15:00 US May Cleveland Fed CPI, 0.5% prev \u8226\'20\'22 18:00 US May Federal Budget USD, -120.00 bln f'cast, 308.00 bln prev Looking Ahead - Events, Other Releases (GMT) \u8226\'20\'22 13:45 Pre-recorded video message by \uc2 ECB\uc2 's \uc2 Christine Lagarde\uc2  at the Institute for Law and Finance of Goethe University \u8226\'20\'22 15:00 \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of Cleveland\uc2  issues Median CPI for May Commentary and Analysis EUR/USD and the beauty of mathematics \u8226\'20\'22 In 2022 EUR/USD sank from 1.1495 peak to 1.0349 low \u8226\'20\'22 Ahead June \uc2 ECB\uc2  meeting pair rallied \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/USD reached 1.0787 (38.2% 1.1495-1.0349) \u8226\'20\'22 It has subsequently dropped reaching 1.0590 EBS \u8226\'20\'22 Thanks to \uc2 ECB\uc2  speculation traders tripled bets on a rise \u8226\'20\'22 Long liquidation may fuel drop towards 1.0522 and 1.0355 targets \u8226\'20\'22 A simple EUR/USD strategy for the year ahead USD/JPY dips as market frets about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  \u8226\'20\'22 Fin Min Suzuki warned against any rapid fluctuations in yen \u8226\'20\'22 Rare govt, \uc2 BOJ\uc2  joint statement highlights \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk \u8226\'20\'22 Yen warnings lifts the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from 2-decade lows \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY has dropped from 134.48 to 133.37, on Friday, EBS data shows \u8226\'20\'22 Recall USD/JPY registered a 20-year peak at 134.56 on Thursday \u8226\'20\'22 USD/JPY chart shows a market on course to test 2002 135.20 peak \u8226\'20\'22 EUR/JPY's 30/60-day long correlations with USD/JPY well above +0.50 \u8226\'20\'22 The two \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs close in the same direction more often than not GBP/USD drops towards Tuesday's low pre-U.S. CPI data \u8226\'20\'22 Cable falls to 1.2451 ahead of U.S. May inflation data at 1230 GMT \u8226\'20\'22 1.2451 is lowest level since Tuesday (1.2433 was the low that day) \u8226\'20\'22 Drop precedes U.S. May CPI data at 1230 GMT; 8.3% YY f/c, core f/c 5.9% YY \u8226\'20\'22 Hotter than f/c CPI would raise risk of (another) 50 bps Fed hike in Sept \u8226\'20\'22 50 bps Fed hikes expected next week and in July. \uc2 BoE\uc2  rate decision June 16 \u8226\'20\'22 2-year gilt yields rise to new 14-year high AUD/USD pushes recovery envelope from two-week low \u8226\'20\'22 AUD/USD reaches 0.7137 after pushing its recovery envelope from 0.7085 \u8226\'20\'22 0.7085 was two-week low in Asia, as risk aversion weighed on the AUD \u8226\'20\'22 Nasdaq closed down 2.75% Thursday, steepest drop since mid-May \u8226\'20\'22 0.7193 was Thursday's high (before equity losses hurt risk-sensitive AUD) \u8226\'20\'22 Iron ore closed down 1.7% Friday (fourth consecutive down-day) \u8226\'20\'22 U.S. May inflation data due 1230 GMT; 8.3% YY f/c, core CPI f/c 5.9% YY A simple EUR/USD strategy for the year ahead EUR/USD is caught between the push me-pull me affects of U.S. and eurozone monetary policies, something EUR/USD traders should use to hedge for the year ahead. As a consequence of changing Fed policies EUR/USD entered a steep decline from 1.2266 to 1.0349 and then bounced to 1.0787 due to speculation about the extent of \uc2 ECB\uc2  tightening. This fulfilled the minimum criterion (38.2%) for a correction of the drop from 2022's peak at 1.1495 to the year low at 1.0349. EUR/USD has since fallen reaching 1.0611 after the CB detailed its plans. The Fed plans to hike interest rates further than \uc2 ECB\uc2  and crucially will reduce its balance sheet when \uc2 ECB\uc2  will not. The result should be a further EUR/USD decline albeit slowed by \uc2 ECB\uc2  policy. There is cause to expect rallies in advance of \uc2 ECB\uc2  meetings and dips ahead of Fed meetings, and potentially a sizeable recovery ahead of \uc2 ECB\uc2 's Sep 8 meeting if a 50bps hike becomes likely. Recoveries are opportunities to hedge for the deeper decline that will result from greater changes in the U.S. This should result in a ratcheting decline with a series of lower EUR/USD ranges unfolding this year with the current range evolving near 1.05-1.08. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3NGQIWa"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/3NGQIWa}}}\uc2  Yen bears growl as BoJ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  risk rises Yen bears may have to tread more carefully following a rare joint statement from Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank of Japan and Financial Services Agency, which has raised the risk of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "We have seen sharp yen declines and are concerned about recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves", Friday's joint statement said, with top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Masato Kanda saying Tokyo "will respond flexibly with all options on the table". The yen strengthened on the back of the statement, with USD/JPY dropping to an EBS intra-day low of 133.37. The yen fell steeply earlier this week, with 134.56 marking Thursday's 20-year EBS high for USD/JPY. The probability of the MOF instructing the BoJ to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and buy yen will increase if USD/JPY vaults its 2002 EBS high of 135.20. Monetary policy announcements are scheduled from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and BoJ next week, on Wednesday and Friday (June 17) respectively. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3NVsEzj"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/3NVsEzj}}}\uc2  To read our latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  news and analysis services, click on\par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-6-13T10:44:31.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220610ei6a01mc1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
