\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 BoJ and other authorities warn of weak yen and do not rule out  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 178 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BoJ), the country's finance ministry and \uc2 Financial Services Agency\uc2  on Friday issued a joint statement expressing concern over the rapid depreciation of the yen in recent weeks. On Wednesday, the dollar renewed a more than two-decade high against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In the statement, the authorities did not rule out the possibility of "taking appropriate action," if necessary, to mitigate the movement.\par \par \uc2 The agencies reiterate that they consider it important for the exchange rate to remain stable, in line with the fundamentals, and state that sudden fluctuations are "undesirable.\par \par \uc2 According to the group, the government and \uc2 BoJ\uc2  will work together to monitor trends and the impact on the economy.\par \par \uc2 The yen has entered a loss spiral recently amid the \uc2 Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's insistence on relaxed monetary policy, running counter to tightening in developed peers.\par \par \uc2 BoJ President \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  has even suggested on several occasions that the weak yen is positive for the economy.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220610ei6a00adn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
