\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 5- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  edges closer to  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in yen after rare gov't, cbank joint statement\b0\par\par\uc2 1,064 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2022\par 17:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  says 'concerned' about sharp yen falls\par \par \uc2 * Top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat says 'all options on table'\par \par \uc2 * Tokyo ready to respond appropriately in accordance to G7 policy\par \par \uc2 * Yen fall puts pressure on \uc2 BOJ\uc2  ahead of next week's meeting\par \par \uc2 * Analysts see low chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 BOJ\uc2  policy tweak (Adds U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation report; updates yen levels after U.S. CPI release)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto and Leika Kihara\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 10 (Reuters) - Japan's government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday they were concerned by recent sharp falls in the yen in a rare joint statement, the strongest warning to date that Tokyo could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it plumbs 20-year lows.\par \par \uc2 The statement underscores growing concern among policymakers over the damage that sharp yen depreciation could inflict on Japan's fragile economy by hurting business activity and consumers.\par \par \uc2 But many market players doubt that G7 member Japan will step in soon to directly prop up the yen, a diplomatically fraught and potentially costly course of action that last occurred 20 years ago.\par \par \uc2 After a meeting with his \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (\uc2 BOJ\uc2 ) counterpart, top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Masato Kanda told reporters that Tokyo will "respond flexibly with all options on the table."\par \par \uc2 He declined to say whether Tokyo could negotiate with other countries to jointly step into the market.\par \par \uc2 The G7 has a long standing policy that markets ought to determine \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, but that the group will closely coordinate on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, and that excessive and disorderly exchange-rate moves could hurt growth.\par \par \uc2 "We have seen sharp yen declines and are concerned about recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves," the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 BOJ\uc2  and the \uc2 Financial Services Agency\uc2  said in the joint statement released after their executives' meeting.\par \par \uc2 "We will communicate closely with each country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities and respond appropriately as needed," based on the G7 principles, the statement said.\par \par \uc2 Officials of the three institutions meet occasionally, usually to signal to markets their alarm over sharp market moves. But it is rare for them to issue a joint statement with explicit warnings over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.\par \par \uc2 The statement came hours ahead of the release of the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2 's twice-annual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation report, which kept Japan on a list of 12 countries whose \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  practices merit "close attention." It took note of the recent yen weakness, which it attributed largely to interest rate differentials owing to the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's continued policy accommodation.\par \par \uc2 The yen briefly rallied to 133.37 yen per dollar after Tokyo's statement, but retraced most of that after a stronger-than-expected reading of U.S. inflation signaled more aggressive rate increases ahead from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 , which are likely to further widen the rate differentials hanging over the yen. It was last at 134.15.\par \par \uc2 "Tokyo could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the yen slides below 135 to the dollar and starts going into a free fall. That's when Tokyo really needs to step in," said Atsushi Takeda, chief economist at Itochu Economic Research Institute in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "But Washington won't join so it will be solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For the United States, there's really no merit in joining Tokyo on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The yen's sharp declines have inflated already rising raw material import costs, jacking up households' living costs and putting pressure on the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  to address creeping inflation.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  and the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  are both scheduled to hold policy meetings next week.\par \par \uc2 With the Japanese economy still much weaker than its peers, the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  is widely expected to maintain its ultra-easy policy next week. But it will face the dilemma of having to stick with low rates, even though it could fuel further yen declines.\par \par \uc2 "I don't think today's statement would have a direct impact on the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's policy meeting next week," said Hiroshi Ugai, chief Japan economist at JPMorgan Securities. "There are limits to what the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  can do."\par \par \uc2 BAR FOR \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  IS HIGH\par \par \uc2 Unlike other major central banks which are flagging aggressive interest rate hikes to tackle inflation, the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  has repeatedly committed to keeping rates low, making Japanese assets less attractive for investors.\par \par \uc2 That increasing policy divergence sent the yen down 15% against the dollar since early March and within striking distance of 135.20 hit on Jan. 31, 2002. A break past that would be its lowest since October 1998.\par \par \uc2 Underscoring growing public sensitivity to rising living costs, \uc2 BOJ\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  was forced to apologise on Tuesday for a remark a day earlier that households were becoming more accepting of price rises.\par \par \uc2 "What can potentially slow the pace of depreciation is a change in policy but right now it looks like there is no indication that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  is concerned about inflation or the impact of the weak yen on that," said Moh Siong Sim, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Bank of Singapore\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It (the joint statement) is more of a verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and I\u8217\'20\'19m not sure whether it will amount to any action and won\u8217\'20\'19t have any impact on the yen," he said, adding the bar for actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets remains very high.\par \par \uc2 Given the economy's heavy reliance on exports, Japan has historically focused on arresting sharp rises in the yen and taken a hands-off approach on yen falls.\par \par \uc2 The last time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in 1998, when the Asian financial crisis triggered a yen sell-off and a rapid capital outflow from the region. Before that, Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to counter yen falls in 1991-1992. Its last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of any kind was in 2011, but that was to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  report, which had no reference to Friday's statement from Tokyo, credited Japan for its transparency about its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  but cautioned that \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be rare events with ample advance notice.\par \par \uc2 "Treasury's firm expectation is that in large, freely traded exchange markets, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be reserved only for very exceptional circumstances with appropriate prior consultations," the report said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto and Leika Kihara; Additional reporting by Kantaro Komiya and Daniel Leussink in Tokyo and Dan Burns in New York; Editing by Kim Coghill and Chizu Nomiyama) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-6-10T16:55:13.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220610ei6a010vt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
