\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar up as hot U.S. inflation data backs case for Fed rate hikes\b0\par\par\uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2022\par 16:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Gasoline, food prices boost U.S. consumer inflation in May\par \par \uc2 * Rare joint statement from \uc2 BOJ\uc2  and govt helps yen (Updates prices, market activity, comments to U.S. market open; previous LONDON)\par \par \uc2 By Saqib Iqbal Ahmed\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, June 10 (Reuters) - The dollar rose to a near four-week high against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, after data showed U.S. consumer prices accelerated in May, suggesting the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  may have to continue with interest rate hikes through September to combat inflation.\par \par \uc2 In the 12 months through May, the CPI increased 8.6% after rising 8.3% in April. Economists had hoped that the annual CPI rate peaked in April.\par \par \uc2 The inflation report was published ahead of an anticipated second 50 basis points rate hike from the Fed next Wednesday. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to raise its policy interest rate by an additional half a percentage point in July. It has hiked the overnight rate by 75 basis points since March.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation is now at a 40-year high with little evidence that it has peaked," said John Doyle, vice president of dealing and trading at Monex USA.\par \par \uc2 "Stocks are extending losses on the expectation the Fed could find the scope to speed up rate hikes. The greenback is gaining on policy divergence and risk-off trading," Doyle said.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Dollar \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Index, which tracks the greenback against six other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was 0.7% higher at 104.02, its highest since May 17, and within sight of 105.01, the two-decade high touched in mid-May.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's gains were broad based with the safe-haven Japanese yen the one major exception.\par \par \uc2 The yen, which has weakened this year on traders' bets that the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  will stick with its ultra-accommodative policy stance, was about 0.11% higher against the greenback after the Japanese government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a rare joint statement, expressed concern about its slide to hit two-decade lows. The dollar was last at 134.18 yen.\par \par \uc2 After a meeting with his \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (\uc2 BOJ\uc2 ) counterpart, the country's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat Masato Kanda told reporters that Tokyo will take appropriate action as needed, a sign \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be edging closer to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in a bid to arrest the yen's declines.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was up 0.81% against the Swiss franc at 0.9883 francs after the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  on Friday said Switzerland continued to exceed its thresholds for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation under a 2015 U.S. trade law, but refrained from branding it a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator.\par \par \uc2 With the U.S. inflation data knocking investors' risk appetite, the risk-sensitive Australian dollar reversed direction to trade down 0.43% on the day.\par \par \uc2 Sterling fell 1.0% to $1.2375 and was set for a second consecutive week of declines as Britain's gloomy economic outlook left investors on edge.\par \par \uc2 In cryptocurrencies, bitcoin slipped 2.4% to $29,382.74, as the world's largest digital \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by market value continued to struggle to overcome a bout of selling pressure that has taken it below the $30,000 level in recent sessions.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Saqib Iqbal Ahmed; editing by David Evans) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-6-10T15:10:58.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220610ei6a02jll\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
