\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen soars on authorities'  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  warning\b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jun 10 (Reuters) - The yen rose on Friday after the government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expressed concern in an unusual joint statement about its recent slide to two-decade lows, while the dollar rose ahead of key U.S. inflation data.\par \par \uc2 * After meeting with his counterpart at the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , Masato Kanda - the country's top \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat - told the media that Tokyo will take the necessary measures, indicating that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be closer to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in an attempt to halt the yen's plunge.\par \par \uc2 * The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been hit by traders betting that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  will maintain its ultra-loose policy just as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and other central banks accelerate their tightening to control rising inflation.\par \par \uc2 * "Usually, if you look at the behavior of the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , if they say they're going to take appropriate action, that's considered the maximum level of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  that they apply before physical \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . So, for now, they've gone as far as they can go," said \uc2 Adam Cole\uc2  of \uc2 RBC Capital Markets\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The yen rose as much as 0.7% in the session to 133.37 yen per dollar before stabilizing at 133.79. On Thursday, it weakened to 134.56 units, a level not seen since early 2002.\par \par \uc2 * The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also rebounded against the euro. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave up 0.8% to 141.65 yen.\par \par \uc2 * On the other hand, the dollar appreciated as traders prepared for US inflation data that could affect the Fed's tightening path.\par \par \uc2 * The dollar index, which compares the greenback to a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , gained 0.2% to 103.52 units, extending the week's gains as growth concerns encourage investors to seek safety in the US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 * The euro subtracted 0.3%, to $1.0587, after touching $1.0611 earlier in the session, its lowest since May 23.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tommy Wilkes; additional reporting by Alun John and Dhara Ranasinghe; edited in Spanish by Carlos Serrano)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220610ei6a008gb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
