\par\par \b \uc2 TIMELINE-History of  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  markets\b0\par\par\uc2 537 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2022\par 10:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 June 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  escalated its warnings on Friday against sharp falls in the yen, expressing "concern" over the moves in a rare joint statement by the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , leaving investors wary about the potential for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 It is more than a decade since \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and more than two decades since it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Here is a timeline of selected moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 1973 - Japanese monetary authorities decide to let the yen float freely against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 1985 - The Group of Five industrial nations, the predecessor to the G7, sign the Plaza Accord in which they agree that the dollar is overvalued and that they will move to weaken it.\par \par \uc2 1987 - In February, six of the G7 nations sign the Louvre Accord, which aims to stabilise \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and halt the dollar's broad decline.\par \par \uc2 1988 - On Jan. 4, the dollar falls to a post World War Two low of 120.45 yen in Tokyo trade. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars and sell yen.\par \par \uc2 1991 - 1992 - \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the yen, selling U.S. dollars.\par \par \uc2 1993 - Bank of Japan sells yen through much of the year to curb its strength.\par \par \uc2 April 1994 - August 1995 - Dollar sinks to a record low against the German mark and a post-war low against the yen. The United States \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly, often with Japanese and European central banks, to prop up the greenback.\par \par \uc2 1997 - 1998 - The Asian financial crisis sees the yen weaken to nearly 148 to the dollar in August, even after U.S. authorities join the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  to buy yen.\par \par \uc2 January 1999 to April 2000 - \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  sells yen at least 18 times, including once via the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and once via the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , due to worries a strong yen will choke off an economic recovery. Yen continues to strengthen.\par \par \uc2 Sept 2001 - \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen after the Sept. 11 attacks in the United States. The \uc2 ECB\uc2  and New York Federal Reserve both operate on behalf of the \uc2 BOJ\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 May-June, 2002 - \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen, often supported by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and \uc2 ECB\uc2 . The yen continues to gain.\par \par \uc2 March 2004 - The end of a 15-month campaign to curb the yen's rise in which Japan spends a total of 35 trillion yen, or more than $300 billion, on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sept. 15, 2010 - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in six years, selling yen to stem a rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the dollar hits a 15-year-low at 82.87 yen.\par \par \uc2 March 18, 2011 - G7 nations jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen strength when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spikes to a record high in the aftermath of a massive earthquake, on speculation that Japanese firms would repatriate foreign assets to pay for reconstruction.\par \par \uc2 Aug and Oct - 2011 - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb gains that officials fear threaten to derail recovery from an economic slump triggered by the March earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \uc2 (Compiled by Tom Westbrook) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-6-10T09:12:20.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220610ei6a012w1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
