\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  repeats warning on sliding yen, keeps mum on  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  chance\b0\par\par\uc2 589 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2022\par 09:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Finmin Suzuki refrains from commenting on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Yen hit fresh 20-year low vs dollar this week\par \par \uc2 * Weak yen pushes up import costs for resource-scarce Japan (Adds MOF-BOJ-FSA meeting in paragraph 3)\par \par \uc2 By Daniel Leussink and Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 10 (Reuters) - Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  on Friday refrained from commenting on the possibility of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem a weak yen, while maintaining his warning against any rapid fluctuations.\par \par \uc2 The latest jaw-boning came a day after the yen hit a fresh 20-year low against the dollar and a seven-year trough against the euro on expectations the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (\uc2 BOJ\uc2 ) will continue to lag behind other major central banks in exiting stimulus policy.\par \par \uc2 Senior officials from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 BOJ\uc2  and banking regulator \uc2 Financial Services Agency\uc2  would meet on Friday from 4 p.m. (0700GMT) to discuss global market developments, the finance ministry said.\par \par \uc2 The weak yen trend has boosted the prices of imported commodities and pushed up the cost of living for resource-deficient Japan.\par \par \uc2 "I won't comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, including the question (of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) to avoid causing any impact from an offhand comment," Suzuki told reporters when asked about the possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "What's most important is \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability as rapid fluctuations are not desirable," Suzuki told a news conference, repeating the official line.\par \par \uc2 "We will continue to carefully watch \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market movements and their impact on Japan's economy with a sense of urgency."\par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday weakened to a fresh 20-year low of 134.56 yen per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities were likely left in a bind over the yen's slide, said Daisaku Ueno, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not working, while it has not reached a danger zone around 145 yen that I think warrants actual \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Ueno said.\par \par \uc2 The yen has lost about 14% against the dollar so far this year. It last traded at about 133.88 yen per dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  in theory could take unilateral action by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while giving U.S. authorities advanced notice of such a move, Ueno said.\par \par \uc2 "But that would upset (\uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  Secretary \uc2 Janet) Yellen\uc2  who is a firm believer of market-determined exchange rates, particularly at a time when the U.S. is battling rising inflation," he added.\par \par \uc2 However, despite repeating verbal warnings against the yen's recent weakening, Japanese authorities remain in no mood to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market, partly because a strong U.S. dollar suggests the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide is due to fundamental factors.\par \par \uc2 A government source with knowledge of the matter told Reuters on condition of anonymity that the velocity of the yen's move would matter more than any particular levels in judging the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Suzuki on Friday said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government would respond appropriately based on the \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  agreement on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There is no clear consensus among analysts on the trigger point for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some investors had previously seen 125 yen to the dollar as a trigger for action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - the level known as the "Kuroda line" after \uc2 BOJ\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  signalled caution when the yen last reached that mark in 2015.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Daniel Leussink and Tetsushi Kajimoto; Editing by Chang-Ran Kim & Shri Navaratnam) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-6-10T08:22:21.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220610ei6a00m2h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
