\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -U.S. dollar hits more than 2-year high on aggressive Fed hike outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,009 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2022\par 21:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Adds new comment, updates prices)\par     * Euro falls on mixed comments from \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials\par     * U.S. dollar index hits fresh 25-mth high after Powell comments\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , U.S. like discussed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -TBS TV\par     * Sterling falls to lowest since Oct 2020 vs dollar\par     * Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par     By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss\par     NEW YORK, April 22 (Reuters) - The dollar surged to a more than two-year high on Friday, continuing to\par draw support from Federal Reserve Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2 's comments on Thursday that seemed to back a half a\par percentage point tightening at next month's policy meeting, as well as his remarks on a likely consecutive\par rate hikes this year.\par     The dollar index, a gauge of the greenback's value against six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , hit 101.33, the highest\par since March 2020, It was last up 0.6% at 101.16, the largest daily percentage gain since mid-March.\par So far this year, the dollar index has gained 5.7%.\par     "The macro fundamentals are still pointing to a higher dollar as short-term Treasury yields vs\par comparable maturity on sovereign yields are positive and inflation is high globally," said Stan Shipley,\par fixed income strategist, at Evercore ISI in New York.\par     "These macro drivers work well until the dollar reaches a level where economic growth is significantly\par impaired and the credit worthiness of \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. government\f28 \uc2 \f2  debt is suspect," he added.\par     Powell on Thursday said a half-point interest rate increase "will be on the table" when U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meets on May 3-4.\par     Fed funds futures have started to price in a third 50-basis-point hike in July, after the same\par increase in May and June, and nearly 250 basis points of cumulative increases in 2022.\par     "Even if the Fed does back-to-back-to-back 50 basis-point hikes, that's still at a rate that is at the\par bottom end or below neutral," said Calvin Tse, head of Americas Developed Markets Strategy (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Rates,\par Equities), at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  in New York.\par     "They likely don't feel that it's excessive tightening because even after these hikes are put in place,\par policy will still be loose, still accommodative."\par     Across the Atlantic, the euro fell 0.4% to $1.0792, after \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials sent\par mixed policy signals.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christine Lagarde\f28 \uc2 \f2  struck a dovish tone on Thursday by saying the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might need\par to cut its growth outlook a day after \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  dove \f28 \uc2 \f2 Luis de Guindos\f28 \uc2 \f2  joined some policymakers in calling for an\par early end of the bank's asset buying scheme coupled with a rate rise in July.\par     Investors are also waiting for Sunday's run-off of French presidential elections between incumbent\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Emmanuel Macron\f28 \uc2 \f2  and far-right challenger \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marine Le Pen\f28 \uc2 \f2 , with the latest polls showing Macron winning with\par 55% of the votes.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Le Pen\f28 \uc2 \f2 's win could provoke tensions with European allies and weigh on the euro, analysts said. \par     Sterling fell against the dollar to its lowest since November 2020 after sales data and recent\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  comments signalled a possible slowdown in the expected rate hike\par path.\par     The pound fell 1.5% against the dollar to $1.2832a, after hitting $1.2830, the lowest since\par October 2020.\par     Against the yen, the dollar rose 0.2% to 128.55 yen. The yen is still within striking distance of its\par weakest level since April 2002 at 129.43 yen per dollar hit on Wednesday.\par     Since the beginning of the year, the yen has lost more than 10% of its value against a resurgent dollar.\par A weak yen has raised the cost of import prices such as commodities, which are still priced in dollars.\par     Traders overall remained wary of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from Japanese monetary officials to strengthen the yen.\par     Japanese television broadcaster \f28 \uc2 \f2 TBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported on Friday that Japan and the United States likely discussed\par the idea of coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem further yen falls during a bilateral finance leaders'\par meeting.\par     Japanese Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shunichi Suzuki\f28 \uc2 \f2  described recent yen falls as "sharp" and said he agreed with\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  to communicate closely on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves.\par     \par     ========================================================\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 3:01PM (1901 GMT)\par  Description      RIC         Last           U.S. Close  Pct Change     YTD Pct       High Bid    Low Bid\par                                               Previous                   Change                   \par                                               Session                                             \par  Dollar index                 101.1900       100.6300    +0.58%         5.778%        +101.3300   +100.4700\par  Euro/Dollar                  $1.0788        $1.0831     -0.40%         -5.11%        +$1.0851    +$1.0771\par  Dollar/Yen                   128.5750       128.3750    +0.17%         +11.70%       +129.1050   +127.7400\par  Euro/Yen                     138.71         139.06      -0.25%         +6.44%        +139.4800   +138.2700\par  Dollar/Swiss                 0.9568         0.9533      +0.37%         +4.90%        +0.9592     +0.9530\par  Sterling/Dollar              $1.2826        $1.3028     -1.54%         -5.16%        +$1.3035    +$1.2823\par  Dollar/Canadian              1.2720         1.2584      +1.08%         +0.61%        +1.2725     +1.2569\par  Aussie/Dollar                $0.7238        $0.7371     -1.79%         -0.41%        +$0.7377    +$0.7235\par  Euro/Swiss                   1.0320         1.0325      -0.05%         -0.45%        +1.0353     +1.0308\par  Euro/Sterling                0.8409         0.8317      +1.11%         +0.11%        +0.8412     +0.8313\par  NZ                           $0.6630        $0.6734     -1.57%         -3.16%        +$0.6736    +$0.6627\par  Dollar/Dollar                                                                                    \par  Dollar/Norway                8.9575         8.8915      +0.66%         +1.60%        +8.9610     +8.8835\par  Euro/Norway                  9.6646         9.6256      +0.41%         -3.48%        +9.6776     +9.6062\par  Dollar/Sweden                9.5439         9.5134      -0.09%         +5.83%        +9.5576     +9.4611\par  Euro/Sweden                  10.2954