\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -U.S. dollar rallies to more than 2-year high on steep Fed rate hike outlook\b0\par\par\uc2 1,029 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2022\par 18:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Fixes typo in headline to "high" instead of "hike")\par     * Euro falls on mixed comments from \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials\par     * U.S. dollar index hits fresh 25-month high after Powell\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , U.S. like discussed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  -TBS TV\par     * Sterling falls to lowest since Oct 2020 vs \par     * Graphic: World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/2RBWI5E}}}\uc2 \f2 \par \par     By Gertrude Chavez-Dreyfuss and Stefano Rebaudo\par     NEW YORK, April 22 (Reuters) - The dollar surged to a more than two-year high on Friday, continuing to\par draw support from Federal Reserve Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerome Powell\f28 \uc2 \f2 's comments on Thursday that more or less backed a half\par a percentage point tightening at next month's policy meeting, including consecutive rate increases this\par year.\par     The dollar index, a gauge of the greenback's value against six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , hit 101.6, the highest\par since March 2020, It was last up 0.4% at 100.99. So far this year, the dollar has gained 5.7%.\par     Powell said a half-point interest rate increase "will be on the table" when U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  meets on\par May 3-4.\par     Fed funds futures have started to price in a third 50 basis-point hike in July, after the same\par increase in May and June, AND nearly 248 basis points of cumulative increases in 2022.\par     "Even if the Fed does back-to-back-to-back 50 basis-point hikes, that's still at a rate that is at the\par bottom end or below neutral," said Calvin Tse, head of Americas Developed Markets Strategy (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Rates,\par Equities), at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  in New York.\par     "Even if the Fed is doing that, they likely don't feel that it's excessive tightening because even after\par these hikes are put in place, policy will still be loose, still accommodative," he added.\par     Across the Atlantic, the euro fell 0.4% to $1.0793, after \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials sent\par mixed policy signals.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christine Lagarde\f28 \uc2 \f2  struck a dovish tone on Thursday by saying the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might need\par to cut its growth outlook a day after \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  dove \f28 \uc2 \f2 Luis de Guindos\f28 \uc2 \f2  joined some policymakers in calling for an\par early end of the bank's asset buying scheme coupled with a rate rise in July.\par     Matthew Ryan, senior market analyst at Ebury said "several \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  members were open to a rate hike in July,\par but Lagarde's comments continued to be non-committal." \par     "Frankly, we think the \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  risks falling quite significantly behind the curve," he added.\par     Investors are also waiting for Sunday's run-off of French presidential elections between incumbent\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Emmanuel Macron\f28 \uc2 \f2  and far-right challenger \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marine Le Pen\f28 \uc2 \f2 , with the latest polls showing Macron winning with\par 55% of the votes.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Le Pen\f28 \uc2 \f2 's win could provoke tensions with European allies and weigh on the euro, analysts said. \par     Sterling fell against the dollar to its lowest since November 2020 after sales data and recent\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  comments signalled a possible slowdown in the expected monetary\par policy tightening path.\par     The pound fell 1.4% against the dollar to $1.2844a, after hitting $1.2839, the lowest since\par October 2020.\par     The Japanese yen was flat against the dollar at 129.37 but still within striking distance of its weakest\par level since April 2002 at 129.43 yen per dollar hit on Wednesday.\par     Since the beginning of the year, the yen has lost more than 10% of its value against a resurgent dollar.\par A weak yen has raised the cost of import prices such as commodities, which are still priced in dollars.\par     Traders remained wary of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from Japanese monetary officials  to strengthen the yen.\par     Japanese television broadcaster \f28 \uc2 \f2 TBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  reported on Friday that Japan and the United States likely discussed\par the idea of coordinated \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem further yen falls during a bilateral finance leaders'\par meeting.\par     Japanese Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shunichi Suzuki\f28 \uc2 \f2  described recent yen falls as "sharp" and said he agreed with\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  Secretary \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  to communicate closely on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  moves.\par     The Chinese offshore yuan fell 0.9% to a fresh 12-month low of 6.548 yuan per dollar in London trade\par  and looked set for its worst week in more than 2-1/2 years.\par     Market participants wondered if this week's fall was a policy response to counter the economic slowdown.\par \par     \par     ==================================================