\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 , U.S. likely discussed joint  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  to buy yen: media\b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara and Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Apr 22 (Reuters) - Japan and the United States probably discussed the idea of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt further yen falls during a meeting of finance chiefs from the two countries, Japanese television network \uc2 TBS\uc2  reported on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The report, citing a Japanese government source, came after Japan's Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  described the yen's recent falls as "sharp" and said he agreed with \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  to maintain close communication on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movements.\par \par \uc2 "We confirmed that the monetary authorities of the two countries will communicate closely, aligning with the exchange rate principles agreed among G7 and G20 members," Suzuki told reporters after a meeting with Yellen in Washington in the context of the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 's spring meetings.\par \par \uc2 Suzuki said he explained to Yellen that the yen's recent declines were pronounced, but declined to comment on whether the two officials discussed the idea of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a report from Washington, \uc2 TBS\uc2  said Suzuki and Yellen likely discussed joint monetary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during their talks.\par \par \uc2 "It seems that the U.S. side would consider the idea," \uc2 TBS\uc2  said, citing the government source. Still, Washington will find it difficult to acquiesce to yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it would drive down the dollar and accelerate an already runaway U.S. inflation reported \uc2 TBS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The yen has plunged to two-decade lows against the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continues to defend its ultra-low rate policy in contrast to growing signs that the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  will decide on an aggressive rate hike.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Leika Kihara; Additional reporting by Daniel Leussink and Kantaro Komiya. Edited in Spanish by Marion Giraldo.)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220422ei4m00fa5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
