\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 , U.S. likely discussed joint yen-buying  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  - media\b0\par\par\uc2 597 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2022\par 16:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Reuters) -\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the United States likely discussed the idea of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem further yen falls during a bilateral finance leaders' meeting, Japanese television broadcaster \uc2 TBS\uc2  reported on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The report, citing a Japanese government source, came after Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  described recent yen falls as "sharp" and said he agreed with \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  Secretary \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  to communicate closely on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.\par \par \uc2 "We confirmed that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities of both countries will communicate closely, aligning with the exchange-rate principles agreed among the G7 and G20 members," Suzuki told reporters after the meeting with Yellen in Washington D.C. on the sidelines of the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  gatherings.\par \par \uc2 Suzuki said he explained to Yellen that recent yen falls were sharp, but declined to comment on whether the two discussed the idea of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a report from Washington, \uc2 TBS\uc2  said Suzuki and Yellen likely discussed joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during their talks.\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. side sounded as if it would consider the idea positively," \uc2 TBS\uc2  quoted the government source as saying. Still, Washington will find it hard to consent to yen-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it would drive down the dollar and accelerate already soaring U.S. inflation, \uc2 TBS\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 When approached by Reuters on the report, a \uc2 Japanese finance ministry\uc2  official said he could not comment on whether joint \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was discussed at the meeting.\par \par \uc2 "It's probably hard to get U.S. consent for coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this timing," said Masahiro Ichikawa, chief market strategist at Sumitomo Mitsui DS Asset Management.\par \par \uc2 "If \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  does take place, that could trigger a huge unwinding of positions and push up the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by 2-3 yen in a short period of time."\par \par \uc2 In a statement issued on Friday, the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  said Yellen and Suzuki "discussed financial market developments, including \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and underscored the importance of maintaining previous G7 and G20 commitments on exchange rates."\par \par \uc2 The yen has plunged to two-decade lows against the dollar, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  continuing to defend its ultra-low rate policy in contrast with heightening chances of aggressive rate hikes by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fall halted this week at lows of 129.43 to the dollar on expectations the issue of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be raised at the G7 and the U.S.-Japan finance leaders' meetings.\par \par \uc2 In a G7 statement issued on Thursday, the finance heads said they were closely monitoring markets that have been "volatile," but made no mention of exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 "The government has said rapid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves were undesirable. What we're seeing now with the yen are rapid moves, so we'll monitor moves closely with a sense of urgency," Suzuki told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Investors believe the yen has even further to fall, with most betting that even a government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't be enough to turn around the momentum.\par \par \uc2 "It wouldn't surprise me if they did talk about joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," though Suzuki likely failed to win consent from Yellen, said Daisaku Ueno, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Mitsubishi UFJ Morgan Stanley Securities\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "That's why Suzuki had little to say about what Yellen told him. Given the U.S. battles with rapid inflation through monetary tightening, it's unthinkable Washington will agree to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's call for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Leika Kihara; Additional reporting by Daniel Leussink and Kantaro Komiya; Editing by Himani Sarkar, Christopher Cushing and Toby Chopra) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-4-22T14:27:46.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220422ei4m001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
