\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  boosts defense of yield target, offers to buy debt for four days\b0\par\par\uc2 527 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2022\par 23:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Reuters) -The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  on Wednesday boosted efforts to defend its yield target, making a fresh offer to buy an unlimited amount of the 10-year bonds for four consecutive sessions.\par \par \uc2 The move comes as the yield on the 10-year JGB remained at 0.25%, the upper limit of its target of around zero percent, throughout Wednesday, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's offer to buy an unlimited amount of the 10-year bonds at that rate.\par \par \uc2 "Given recent yield movements on longer-ended notes, we have announced a consecutive unlimited fixed-rate purchase of bonds to achieve our policy to guide the 10-year yield around 0%," the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The rise in yields comes as the yen weakens sharply to two-decade lows against the U.S. dollar amid a relentless widening of Japanese and U.S. yield spreads, prompting markets to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's commitment to its super-easy yield-curve-control policy..\par \par \uc2 The benchmark 10-year Treasury yield climbed to the highest since late 2018 at 2.981% in Tokyo trading on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  has no other choice than to keep offering unlimited purchases of JGBs," said Takafumi Yamawaki, head of Japan fixed income research at JPMorgan Securities.\par \par \uc2 "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows 10-year bond yields to keep going up, its message to the market would become unclear."\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2 's guidance is that it will allow the 10-year yield to move flexibly around its 0% target as long as it stays below the 0.25% upper limit.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BOJ\uc2  accepted all of the 225.1 billion yen ($1.75 billion) in bids it received in Wednesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The bank had also offered to buy unlimited amounts of 10-year bonds at 0.25% in February and made four consecutive days of offers in March.\par \par \uc2 With the Japanese economy still weak and inflation modest, the \uc2 BOJ\uc2  has stressed its resolve to keep policy ultra-loose even as the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  looks set to raise rates aggressively to stem soaring prices.\par \par \uc2 BOJ\uc2  Governor \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2  said on Monday the yen's recent moves had been "quite sharp" and could hurt companies' business plans, offering his strongest warning yet of the risks stemming from the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's depreciation.\par \par \uc2 Minister of Finance \uc2 Shunichi Suzuki\uc2  was more categorical on Tuesday, warning that the damage to the economy from a weakening yen at present is greater than the benefits.\par \par \uc2 The yen sank to near 130 per dollar on Wednesday - a level not seen for two decades - raising the risk of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would buy up large amounts of yen in the open market with its foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.\par \par \uc2 The last time \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in 1998, when the Asian financial crisis triggered a yen sell-off and a rapid capital outflows from the region.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 128.6500 yen)\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Junko Fujita; Additional reporting by Kevin Buckland; Editing by Jacqueline Wong, Bradley Perrett and Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2022-4-20T21:04:45.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020220420ei4k03msd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
