\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Yen halts losing streak on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  worries; euro soars\b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 April 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By Saikat Chatterjee\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Apr 20 (Reuters) - The yen briefly fell on Wednesday to a fresh two-decade low after the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to defend its ultra-low interest rate policy, in contrast to the United States, where bond yields touched new highs.\par \par \uc2 * However, the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded in London trading, as increased nervousness around the verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and growing speculation around an impending bilateral meeting between \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  Secretary Yellen and her Japanese counterpart caused traders to scale back some short bets.\par \par \uc2 * Still, positions in derivatives and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures suggest that the yen's weakness has more room to run.\par \par \uc2 * The Bank of Japan again offered to buy unlimited amounts of Japanese government bonds to curb the rise in 10-year local bond yields, which were touching a tolerance ceiling of 0.25%.\par \par \uc2 * By contrast, the return on Treasury notes hit three-year highs, while that on inflation-linked paper touched positive territory for the first time since March 2020, as comments from monetary policymakers reinforced expectations of aggressive rate hikes in the United States.\par \par \uc2 * The dollar hit 129.43 yen for the first time since April, before slipping 0.9% to 127.82 units.\par \par \uc2 * The euro was another big gainer in London after media reports that some \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers expected a first rate hike as early as July. The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was up 0.6% at $1.0853.\par \par \uc2 * The dollar index, which compares the greenback with six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the yen, matched the previous day's high of 101.03 earlier in the day - a level not seen since March 2020 - before falling to 100.38, a decline of 0.6% on the session.\par \par \uc2 (Edited in Spanish by Carlos Serrano)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220420ei4k00c1u\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \t